  <name>Alpine MTB Map</name>
  <description><![CDATA[A curated open map for gravity mountain biking. Discover top downhill bike parks, enduro trails, and freeride spots worldwide. Each main pin gives what it costs to get up, what the trails are like, and the weather forecast. Blue pins are purpose-built bike parks, dark green pins are natural lift-served spots, and brown pins are the ones you pedal up. A few spots stay ridable in winter. Lines are trail geometries from OpenStreetMap - treat them as indicative, not as a substitute for on-site signage. Compiled July 2026.]]></description>
  <visibility>1</visibility>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Krasnaya Polyana Bike Park (Sochi, Russia)</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Polyana 520 m - valley station of the K1 gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>About 30 km of purpose-built gravity trails between roughly 1,375 m and 540 m, graded green, blue, red and black. The network mixes long flow sections with berms and rhythm features, steep technical lines, drops, wooden features, a skills park and pump track. The lower K1 gondola carries bikes between Polyana 540 and Polyana 960; the Vodopad Polikarya chairlift serves the upper sector.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Bike-pass required from 09:00 to 17:00 and sold at Polyana 540 and 960. Bikes use the external racks on the Krasnaya Polyana K1 gondola and the designated carriers on the Vodopad Polikarya chairlift. Check the live lift and trail status and current tariff before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 May; closed from 01 November (typical summer operating window; snow and maintenance can shorten the upper sector season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>The resort lies within Sochi National Park; access above 960 m may require a separate national-park permit.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Sochi / Adler airport</td><td>Car / taxi</td><td>50-70 min</td></tr><tr><td>Esto-Sadok</td><td>Bus / taxi</td><td>10 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://krasnayapolyanaresort.ru/">official live bike-park and lift status</a>, <a href="https://krasnayapolyanaresort.ru/">official trail overview</a> and <a href="https://krasnayapolyanaresort.ru/rules_bike_park.pdf">official bike-park rules</a>. Lift-top coordinate cross-checked against the published Vodopad Polikarya upper-station coordinate.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>40.266913,43.683213,522</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>krasnaya-polyana-bike-park</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>05-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>11-01</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
