  <Placemark>
    <name>Manzherok Bike Park (Altai, Russia)</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Manzherok 905 m - valley station of the Vostok chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Lift-served downhill and enduro terrain on Malaya Sinyukha above Lake Manzherok. Published descriptions list green, blue, red and black gravity trails with berms, drops, steep turns and wooden skills features. The resort has expanded substantially, so published totals vary from about 7 km for the original downhill park to roughly 13 km for the wider bike-park network.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Vostok chairlift reaches the 1,240 m upper station and connects to descending trails including mapped routes Argut, Maral and Velvet. Bike transport and the applicable downhill tariff should be confirmed with the resort before travelling; the older published bike-park information refers to a dedicated bike pass.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 June; closed from 01 October (typical summer window; current MTB operating dates not published clearly online).<br/>Daily opening hours: check with resort<br/><small>Manzherok has undergone major lift and trail redevelopment. Confirm which gravity trails and bike-carrying lifts are open before travel.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Gorno-Altaysk airport</td><td>Car / taxi</td><td>30-40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Manzherok village</td><td>Car / taxi</td><td>10-15 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.ski.ru/az/resort/524/activity/15218">published Manzherok bike-park overview</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/9729515306">OSM Vostok upper station node 9729515306</a> (ODbL), mapped at 1,240 m and operated by Manzherok.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>85.827724,51.799583,905</coordinates></Point>
