  <Placemark>
    <name>Chimgan - Ugam-Chatkal (Uzbekistan) [no bike lift documented]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Natural Tian Shan enduro and adventure riding above Charvak Reservoir</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Chimgan is the main mountain base near Tashkent, with rocky jeep tracks, shepherd paths, gorge descents and steep natural terrain in the Ugam-Chatkal mountains. It is best approached as a guided backcountry ride rather than a maintained bike park; trail marking and reliable difficulty information are limited.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Pedal access or locally arranged vehicle support. No operating mountain-bike lift is documented. Nearby Amirsoy runs gondolas for sightseeing, but its official summer activity information does not confirm bicycle carriage.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 May; closed from 01 November (average snow-free riding season).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Confirm the route, protected-area rules and any permit requirements with a local guide before riding.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Tashkent</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 30</td></tr><tr><td>Chimgan village</td><td>Bike</td><td>Direct</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.amirsoy.com/en/activities">Amirsoy official activities</a> and <a href="https://visittashkent.uz/tours/tashkent-mountain-tour/">Visit Tashkent mountain-area information</a>. Current MTB infrastructure is not formally documented, so verify locally.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>70.015402,41.559475,1357</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>chimgan-ugam-chatkal</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>expert natural no-lift enduro</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>05-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>11-01</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Jyrgalan Valley MTB (Kyrgyzstan) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Community-based natural mountain biking in the eastern Tian Shan</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Marked village routes include the 7 km Tulpar Tash ride, the 13 km Kok-Bel waterfall route and the 16.6 km Eki Chat loop. Stronger riders can tackle the rough Kok-Bel Pass route, with alpine terrain, river valleys and technical natural sections. Local guesthouses arrange rentals and guides.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Pedal access; no lift. Guided rides and vehicle support can be arranged locally. The destination lists bike rental at 1,320 KGS per day or 660 KGS per half day; confirm current rates.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 June; closed from 01 October (official recommended riding season is June to September).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Mountain weather changes quickly. Carry repair and navigation equipment, and use a local guide for remote routes.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Karakol</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr><tr><td>Jyrgalan village</td><td>Bike</td><td>Direct</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://jyrgalan.com/what-to-do/mountain-biking/">Destination Jyrgalan official mountain-biking guide</a>. Check current trail and rental conditions locally.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>78.500159,42.599493,1647</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>jyrgalan-valley-mtb</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert natural no-lift enduro</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>10-01</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Karakol - Jeti-Oguz MTB (Kyrgyzstan) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Karakol ski base 2400 m - road head above the Karakol gorge, where the descents start</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Karakol is the principal base for forest singletrack, alpine valleys and long natural descents around Jeti-Oguz and the eastern Issyk-Kul region. Riding ranges from approachable valley routes to remote high-pass adventures with substantial climbing and exposed mountain terrain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Pedal access or a locally arranged shuttle; no lift-served bike park is documented. Do not assume that nearby ski lifts carry bicycles. Karakol has bike rental and guiding operators for day rides and supported multi-day trips.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 June; closed from 15 October (average high-country riding season).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Route conditions and river crossings vary. A guide is strongly recommended outside the lower valley network.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Karakol town</td><td>Bike / car up the gorge road</td><td>~40 min by car</td></tr><tr><td>Bishkek</td><td>Car</td><td>~5 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://visitkyrgyzstan.org/karakol-mountain-biking/">Visit Kyrgyzstan Karakol mountain-biking guide</a>. Confirm routes, guides and access before departure.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>78.466210,42.408430,2400</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>karakol-jeti-oguz-mtb</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert natural no-lift enduro</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>10-15</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Saint-George / Mont Chaubert [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mont Chaubert - pedal-up Jura vaudois riding</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Four marked natural descents near Saint-George: Mont Chaubert, Mont Bailly, its eastern variant and La Plagne. Short, rooty and rocky Jura singletrack with no mechanical uplift; climb from Saint-George or arrange a local shuttle. The routes are shared forest paths, so follow local MTB signs and give way to other users.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No bike lift. Pedal up from Saint-George or use a local shuttle. Free access where permitted.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 April; closed from 01 December (typical window; check local conditions and forestry notices).<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Saint-George</td><td>Bike / car</td><td>Local access</td></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train + bike</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://parcjuravaudois.ch/actualite/vtt-dans-le-jura-vaudois/">Parc Jura vaudois MTB information</a>, <a href="https://www.komoot.com/guide/55904/mtb-trails-around-saint-george">Saint-George MTB routes</a> and the individual OpenStreetMap links on each trace. Verify access, trail status and local rules before riding.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>6.275959,46.518879,1073</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
