  <Placemark>
    <name>Lenzerheide - Bike Kingdom Park [from 53 CHF]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lenzerheide 1500 m - valley station of the Rothorn gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Five built lines drop off the Rothorn and all finish back at the valley station: the green FLOWline to find your feet, the red PRIMEline and the wood-built SHOREline through the middle, and the black STYLEline next to the STRAIGHTline, which is the World Cup race track. That is 1 green, 2 red and 3 black in the park proper. Off the park, the Biketicket to RIDE marathon route and the Bike Attack race line run for tens of kilometres down the valley, so a Bike Kingdom pass is worth more than the five lines suggest.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Rothornbahn from Lenzerheide at 1500 m, in two sections to 2865 m; the Urdenbahn links across to Arosa on the same ticket. Day pass 53 CHF adult; the Bike Kingdom pass and the Graubunden regional passes both cover it.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 June; closed from 26 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Chur</td><td>Bus</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Zurich</td><td>Train + bus</td><td>~2h20</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.bikekingdom.ch/en/Bikeparks/Bike-Kingdom-Park">Bike Kingdom Park</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>9.556581,46.740208,1500</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
      <Data name="spot"><value>lenzerheide</value></Data>
      <Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh freeride</value></Data>
