  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Chur: Brambrüeschbahn mountain station (1595 m)</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Brambrueesch 1600 m - top of the Chur cable car</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The valley-floor member of the Bike Kingdom, and the one to pick if the weather up high looks bad. Four built flow trails drop off Brambrueesch back into town: Brambi Flow and Chur Flow are the easy, jumpy ones, Alpen Ride is longer and more natural, and Rock'n'Roll is the rough one. Around 1000 m of descent, straight into a city with trains home.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Covered by the same Bike Kingdom ticket, from 53 CHF. The cable car starts inside the city, so there is no bus and no transfer at the far end.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 May; closed from 2 November (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train</td><td>~3h45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.chur.graubuenden.ch/en/activities/summer/mountain-biking">Chur tourism</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-gray</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>9.516227,46.828967,1594</coordinates></Point>
