  <Placemark>
    <name>Bike Park Valbirse [from 15 CHF]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Pontenet 765 m - valley station of the Les Orvales surface lift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Compact, community-maintained bike park featuring technical singletracks, flow sections with tabletop jumps, bermed turns, and short jump lines (Expresso, Chilli Peppers, Schtroumpfette). Small scale but well-loved local spot in the Bernese Jura.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Surface T-bar drag lift (Téléski Les Orvales). Operating hours are managed by the local club; day pass typically costs around 15-25 CHF.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from late April/early May; closed from late October (typical window; check the local club).<br/>Daily opening hours: variable<br/><small>Check the local club schedule before visiting.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train</td><td>~1h50</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.bikeparkvalbirse.ch/en/">BikePark Valbirse</a>, <a href="https://www.bikeparkvalbirse.ch/en/horaires-et-tarifs">official hours and prices</a>, <a href="https://www.valbirse.ch/1211-culture-loisirs-teleski-bikepark">Commune de Valbirse</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
