  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Andermatt: railway station</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Gutsch 2344 m - top of the Gutsch-Express</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>High, bare and properly alpine - the SkiArena runs from the Gemsstock at nearly 3000 m across the Oberalp to Sedrun. The riding here is route-based rather than park-based: Oberalp Bike (205) is the classic loop over the pass, and Cavorgia Bike (207) carries on towards Sedrun. Add the Gottardo Bike and Furka Bike stages and you have a week of it. Little shelter and a short season: it can snow in August.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Andermatt+Sedrun+Disentis sells summer bike and hiking day passes; check andermatt-sedrun-disentis.ch for price. Their half-price card covers summer bike day passes as well as winter skiing if you go more than once.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 27 June; closed from 5 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train</td><td>~4h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.andermatt-sedrun-disentis.ch/de/">Andermatt</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-gray</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>8.621960,46.656424,2361</coordinates></Point>
