  <Placemark>
    <name>Bellwald (Goms, above Fiesch) [from 40 CHF]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Bellwald 1625 m - valley station of the Bellwald chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Seven graded lines plus a pumptrack, all on natural ground through forest and open alp rather than machine-shaped dirt: 3 blue (Forest Bump, the family flow line with berms and small jumps, Vast &amp; Furious and Line King), 2 red (Into the Wild and the enduro-style Lord of the Rims), and 2 black (Sliderman, a technical play trail through rock and roots, and Dirty Cranking, the proper downhill line). One of the better-known lift-served freeride parks in Switzerland, and quiet, because the Goms is a long way up the Rhone.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Two chairlift sections from Bellwald at 1625 m: valley station to Fleschen, then Fleschen to Furggulti. The 2022 six-seater carries bikes on holders. Day pass from 40 CHF.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from mid-June; closed from mid-October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-16:45<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Fiesch station</td><td>Postbus</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Brig</td><td>Train + bus</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.bikeparkbellwald.com/trails">Bike Park Bellwald</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>8.161785,46.428973,1624</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
      <Data name="spot"><value>bellwald</value></Data>
      <Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh freeride rain-resilient</value></Data>
      <Data name="open_from"><value>05-20</value></Data>
      <Data name="closed_from"><value>10-26</value></Data>
      <Data name="price_day"><value>40 CHF</value></Data>
      <mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon>
      <mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility>
    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Bellwald: Bellwald gondola top (2040 m)</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Richinen 2000 m - top of the Bellwald gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One of Switzerland's premier bike parks: Forest Bump (flowtrail), Slider Man (jump line), Vast & Furious (high alpine line), and Dirty Cranking (downhill track used for iXS Downhill Cup). Rich variety of drops, gap jumps, technical root lines, and flow turns. South facing, so it dries fast and rides well into October. Bellwald and the wider Aletsch Arena return as a UCI Enduro World Cup venue in 2026 after hosting the 2025 World Championships enduro races.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Chairlift access (Sesselbahn Bellwald-Richinen). Bike day pass costs approximately 40-48 CHF.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from late May/early June; closed from late October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train + bus</td><td>~2h45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.bellwald.ch/">Bellwald</a> and <a href="https://www.uci.org/pressrelease/the-uci-and-warner-bros-discovery-unveil-the-calendar-for-the-2026-whoop-uci/6FU08VZbYOFKIftHZjLPO7">2026 UCI calendar</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-gray</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>8.166794,46.441362,2077</coordinates></Point>
