  <Placemark>
    <name>Zermatt - Sunnegga [~55 CHF]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Zermatt 1640 m - valley station of the Sunnegga Express funicular</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Signed bike routes rather than a built park, and worth the trip for the setting alone. Three easy ones: the 5.2 km Sunnegga FlowTrail down through Patrullarve and Haueten, the short Moos flow trail off the Matterhorn Express at Furi, and the 12.1 km 4-Lakes tour past Stellisee and Gruensee. Two demanding: the 4.6 km Blauherd-Sunnegga route, which gets tight and technical, and the Stafel-Schoenbielhuette climb, which involves carrying. So 3 easy and 2 hard official routes, plus the network of alpine tracks between them.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The underground Sunnegga Express funicular from the village at 1640 m, continuing by gondola to Blauherd; the Matterhorn Express serves Furi on the other side. Bike day pass about 55 CHF for Sunnegga, more for the higher sections. Zermatt is car-free - park at Taesch and take the shuttle train.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from late June; closed from mid-October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Taesch</td><td>Shuttle train</td><td>~12 min</td></tr><tr><td>Visp</td><td>Train</td><td>~1h10</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.matterhornparadise.ch/en/experience/biking/bike-trails">Zermatt Bergbahnen bike trails</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>7.753170,46.022080,1642</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
      <Data name="spot"><value>zermatt</value></Data>
