    <name>Le Suchet (Jura vaudois) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Le Suchet 1588 m - summit</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Open Jura ridge with descents falling off every side - grassy and fast on the Vaud slope, rockier and steeper towards Baulmes. No signage, no lift queue, big views over the Plateau to the Alps. Best in early summer before the cattle churn the tracks.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Yverdon-les-Bains is 25 min from Lausanne, then a bus to Baulmes or Vuiteboeuf. From there it is roughly 800 m of climbing under your own steam.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 April; closed from 16 November (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train + bus</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://map.geo.admin.ch/">Swiss federal map</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>6.466241,46.772374,1575</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app">
      <Data name="spot"><value>suchet</value></Data>
      <Data name="tags"><value>beginner natural enduro</value></Data>
      <Data name="open_from"><value>04-15</value></Data>
      <Data name="closed_from"><value>11-16</value></Data>
      <mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon>
      <mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility>
    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Grand Cunay / Col du Marchairuz [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Grand Cunay 1566 m</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Classic Jura vaudois ridge riding above the Vallee de Joux. Rolling limestone pasture, dry-stone walls and forest singletrack, with long low-gradient descents rather than steep ones. Quiet on weekdays; the Parc Jura vaudois rules ask you to stay on the tracks.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift, and a sparse bus timetable: check the Bière or Le Brassus connections to the Col du Marchairuz before committing. Many people ride up from Bière instead.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 April; closed from 16 November (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train + bus</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://map.geo.admin.ch/">Swiss federal map</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>6.276140,46.572227,1565</coordinates></Point>
