  <Placemark>
    <name>Durmitor - Zabljak (Montenegro) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>High-alpine adventure riding from Zabljak</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Durmitor offers demanding backcountry riding on rough mountain roads, shepherd tracks and permitted routes around the plateau, Tara canyon and Sinjajevina. The appeal is remote scenery and long natural days, not built downhill trails.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No verified bike uplift: climb under your own power or arrange vehicle support with a local guide. This is a protected national park, so confirm the exact bicycle route and current restrictions before riding.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 June; closed from 01 November (typical snow-free window).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Weather, snow and national-park access can change quickly.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Podgorica</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr><tr><td>Zabljak</td><td>Bike</td><td>direct</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.montenegro.travel/en/unique-montenegro/national-parks-of-montenegro/durmitor-national-park">Montenegro Tourism</a> and its official biking-route publications. Confirm permitted access locally.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>19.118866,43.155777,1435</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>durmitor-zabljak</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>expert natural no-lift enduro</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>11-01</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Kolasin - Bjelasica and Sinjajevina (Montenegro) [no bike lift documented]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Natural mountain-bike base around Kolasin</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Guided routes explore Bjelasica, Sinjajevina and the approaches to Biogradska Gora, ranging from rolling pasture and jeep track to long rocky backcountry descents. It is an adventure/enduro base rather than a signed bike park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No summer bike uplift was verified despite the nearby ski lifts. Pedal the routes or arrange guide and vehicle support in Kolasin.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 May; closed from 01 November (typical snow-free window).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Confirm route access, fire restrictions and vehicle support locally.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Podgorica</td><td>Train / car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Kolasin</td><td>Bike / shuttle</td><td>~20 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://kolasin.me/en/">Kolasin Tourism Organisation</a>. Check current guided routes and access.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>19.651373,42.814716,1731</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>kolasin-bjelasica</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert natural no-lift enduro</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>05-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>11-01</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
