  <Placemark>
    <name>Vodno - Skopje (North Macedonia) [gondola normally carries bikes]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Millennium Cross 1066 m - natural singletrack above Skopje</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A dense local network drops through forest from the Vodno summit toward Skopje and west toward Matka Canyon. Lines range from fast flow to steep, rocky expert singletrack; this is natural shared mountain riding, not a managed bike park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The gondola from Middle Vodno normally has bicycle hooks, with a pedal or bus climb to its base. Major maintenance reportedly closes it through much of summer 2026, so verify reopening before relying on uplift.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 September; closed from 01 December (conservative 2026 post-maintenance window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-18:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; check gondola status and bicycle carriage before travel.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Skopje centre</td><td>Bus + gondola / bike</td><td>~40 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://bikemacedonia.com/tours/trails-of-vodno/">Bike Macedonia</a> and current local gondola maintenance reporting. Trails are shared; ride considerately.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-green</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>21.394421,41.965020,1052</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>vodno</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>expert natural dh enduro</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>09-15</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>12-01</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Mavrovo National Park (North Macedonia) [no bike lift documented]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Marked mountain-bike routes around Mavrovo Lake and Bistra</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>North Macedonia's largest national park contains marked and unmarked mountain-bike routes through Bistra, Korab foothills, forest and high pasture. Historical freeride/flow development exists near the resort, but current lift-assisted bike operation could not be verified.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Plan on pedal access or a booked local shuttle. National-park rules apply, and high fire danger can trigger mandatory registration or complete forest-access restrictions.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 April; closed from 01 December (typical snow-free window, subject to fire closures).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Check park notices and register when required before entering forest land.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Skopje</td><td>Car / bus</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>Mavrovo</td><td>Bike</td><td>direct</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://npmavrovo.org.mk/en/%D0%BF%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B8%D1%80%D0%B0%D1%9A%D0%B5-%D0%B8-%D0%BF%D0%BB%D0%B0%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8-%D0%B2%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BE%D1%81%D0%B8%D0%BF%D0%B5%D0%B4%D0%B8%D0%B7%D0%B0%D0%BC/">Mavrovo National Park MTB guidance</a> and current park notices.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>20.752707,41.698649,1253</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>mavrovo</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert natural no-lift enduro freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>04-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>12-01</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Peja - Rugova and Accursed Mountains (Kosovo) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Natural enduro and adventure riding from Rugova Canyon</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Kosovo's best-documented mountain-bike destination links Peja, Rugova Canyon and the Accursed Mountains. Mapped routes deliver more than 1700 m of vertical across rocky mule paths, forest singletrack, high pasture and cross-border adventure terrain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No verified mechanical uplift. Pedal from Peja or arrange local guide and vehicle support. Border-crossing and protected-area routes may require permissions, so confirm the exact itinerary.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 May; closed from 01 November (typical snow-free window).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Check weather, border requirements and local trail access.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Peja</td><td>Bike / shuttle</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Pristina</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://pejatourism.org/cycling/">Peja Tourism</a> and its outdoor-activity publications. Confirm routes and permissions locally.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>20.208657,42.663523,760</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>peja-rugova</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>expert natural no-lift enduro</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>05-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>11-01</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Mottolino Bike Park (Livigno) [from 29.50 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mottolino gondola to 2400 m above Livigno</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One of Italy's benchmark gravity parks, with downhill race tracks, accessible flow, North Shore woodwork, a dedicated jump area, drops and large freeride features. It hosted the 2005 MTB World Championships and remains Livigno's harder, park-focused sector.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Mottolino gondola carries bikes. Bike passes start from 29.50 EUR; rentals, workshop and coaching are at the base.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 13 June; closed from 28 September (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Published 2026 hours; check live trail status.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Livigno centre</td><td>Bike / bus</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>St Moritz</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.mottolino.com/en/summer/bikepark/">Mottolino</a>. Prices and operations can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>10.162912,46.526810,2396</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>mottolino</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-13</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>09-28</value></Data><Data name="price_day"><value>29.50 EUR</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Carosello 3000 Mountain Park (Livigno) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Carosello gondola - Livigno's flow and enduro sector</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The western side of Livigno emphasizes long, flowing mountain-bike trails, high-alpine enduro and natural singletrack rather than pure DH. Rolling blue progression, fast red flow and big panoramic descents link Carosello, Costaccia and the Sitas area.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Carosello 3000 and connecting summer lifts carry bikes. Check Livigno for the current area or combined bike pass.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 20 June; closed from 27 September (typical 2026 summer window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical lift hours; verify the operating calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Livigno centre</td><td>Bike / bus</td><td>~15 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.carosello3000.com/it/">Carosello 3000</a> and <a href="https://www.livigno.eu/en/">Livigno Tourism</a>. Verify current lifts and trails.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>10.122804,46.520816,1877</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>carosello-3000</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park enduro freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-20</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>09-27</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Fassa Bike Park (Canazei, Dolomites) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Canazei-Pecol lifts in the Val di Fassa Dolomites</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>18 trails across three mountainsides between Col Rodella and Belvedere, graded from approachable flow to World Series-grade tech; the black line is the one with north shore, jumps and drops. Most of the riding sits around 2000 m, alternating natural ground and shaped sections, with the Sellaronda MTB tour linked in by lift. The district does not publish a per-colour breakdown - grades are signed on the ground.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Eight lifts serve the district, reachable from Campitello, Canazei or Alba; the Canazei-Pecol gondola is the usual start. Passes are sold by the Val di Fassa lift company - check current rates.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 13 June; closed from 28 September (published 2026 Canazei-Pecol dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00<br/><small>Typical lift hours; individual sectors have different calendars.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bolzano</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Canazei</td><td>Bike</td><td>~5 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.fassabike.com/en/bike-park/trails/">Fassa Bike trails</a> and its <a href="https://www.fassabike.com/en/bike-park/aperture-e-costi/">opening times and prices</a>. Verify sector and lift status.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>11.771075,46.476881,1455</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>fassa-bike</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-13</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>09-28</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Bormio Bike Park (Valtellina) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Bormio 2000 lift sector above the Stelvio valley</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A revived high-vertical park with downhill race terrain, fast alpine pistes, shaped flow and technical forest sections. The 2026 reopening also hosts a round of the Internazionali d'Italia Downhill.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Bormio lifts carry bikes to the park; check the operator for current tickets and open sectors.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 18 July; closed from 13 September (2026 opening date and estimated closing window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Closing date and hours are estimates; verify the 2026 calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Tirano</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Bormio</td><td>Bike / lift</td><td>~10 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.bormioski.eu/en/blog/events/bormio-bike-park-reopens-kick-off-the-downhill-season-with-a-special-2-for-1-offer/">Bormio Ski 2026 announcement</a>. Verify current operations.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>10.388393,46.443967,1942</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>bormio-bike-park</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>07-18</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>09-13</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Madebike Park Madesimo (Valchiavenna) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Larici gondola to Alpe Groppera</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A compact Lombardy park specializing in downhill and freeride, with beginner flow, technical wooded gravity tracks, rocks and race lines. The gondola gives fast repeated laps from the pedestrian centre.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Larici gondola carries bikes in under five minutes. Check Skiarea Valchiavenna for the current bike pass.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 20 June; closed from 13 September (2026 opening date and typical closing window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical hours; consult the 2026 lift calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Chiavenna</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Milan</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.madesimo.eu/it/esperienze/madebike-park/">Madesimo Tourism</a>. Verify lift and trail status.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>9.358414,46.436298,1542</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>madebike-madesimo</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-20</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>09-13</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Sanremo - Monte Bignone Enduro (Liguria) [shuttle, natural]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Natural shuttle enduro above the Ligurian coast</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A winter-training classic for elite enduro and downhill riders: steep dry singletrack, loose rock, exposed ridges and technical forest descents drop from Monte Bignone toward Sanremo and the sea. This is an extensive natural network, not a signed bike park.<br/><br/><b>Rain sensitivity</b><br/>Rain-resilient: dry Ligurian singletrack, loose rock and exposed ridges are a dependable wet-spell alternative.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Local operators provide van shuttles; self-powered loops are also possible. Confirm land access and use a local guide for the maze of trails.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 October; closed from 01 June (best cool-season window; riding may be possible year-round).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Shuttles require booking; fire risk and trail access can change.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Nice</td><td>Train / car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr><tr><td>Sanremo</td><td>Shuttle</td><td>~30 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://sanremooutdoor.it/en/mountainbike/">Sanremo Outdoor</a>, which manages the Monte Bignone consortium trails. Confirm routes, access and shuttle arrangements locally.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-green</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>7.733859,43.873521,1294</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>sanremo-enduro</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>expert natural dh enduro freeride rain-resilient</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>10-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>06-01</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Bardonecchia Bike Park (Piedmont) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lift-served gravity across the Bardonecchia ski sectors</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>More than 40 lift-served routes, all signed and graded green, blue, red and black, inside a wider network of over 400 km of trail between 1300 and 3000 m. Downhill, freeride and enduro across open alpine slopes and larch woods, with family progression at one end and long technical race-style descents at the other. One of the biggest western-Alps parks that is still reachable from Turin on a regional train.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer chairlifts carry bikes. Bike park day pass 25 EUR adult in summer 2026, 14 EUR for under-sevens; a single pedestrian return is 11 EUR.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 27 June; closed from 06 September (typical main season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated standard hours; verify the lift calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Turin</td><td>Train</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>Bardonecchia station</td><td>Bike</td><td>~10 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.bardonecchiaski.com/it/bardonecchia-bike-park">Bardonecchia Ski bike park</a> and its <a href="https://www.bardonecchiaski.com/it/attivita/tariffe-estive">summer tariffs</a>. Verify current operations.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.703205,45.078339,1293</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>bardonecchia</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-27</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>09-06</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Sauze d'Oulx Bike Park (Alpi Bike Resort) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sportinia chairlift to Rocce Nere 2420 m</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>More than 1000 m of descent through alpine meadows and larch forest, with long flowing blue and red trails, technical black DH and natural enduro links through the wider Alpi Bike Resort.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Sportinia chairlift carries bikes from Sauze d'Oulx. Day and season products are published by the resort.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 27 June; closed from 06 September (published 2026 opening and typical closing window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical hours; check the 2026 operating calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Turin</td><td>Train + bus / car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>Oulx station</td><td>Bus</td><td>~15 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://sauzedoulx.net/en/summer/freeride/">Sauze d'Oulx</a>. Verify prices and lift status.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.858346,45.027027,1515</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>sauze-doulx</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride season-pass</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-27</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>09-06</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Prato Nevoso Bike Park (Piedmont) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lift-served Maritime Alps bike park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A major northwest Italian park with downhill, freeride and flow lines over open ski terrain and lower woods. Progression trails sit beside technical race tracks, jumps and fast machine-shaped berms.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer chairlifts carry bikes; check Prato Nevoso for current pricing.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 13 June; closed from 27 September (typical summer and weekend window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; confirm open days and lift status.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Turin</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr><tr><td>Cuneo</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.pratonevoso.com/">Prato Nevoso</a>. Verify summer bike operations.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>7.785589,44.255292,1540</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>prato-nevoso</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-13</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>09-27</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Caldirola Bike Park (Piedmont Apennines) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Compact chairlift park on Monte Gropà</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A cult northern-Apennine gravity hill with fast repeated laps, roots, loam, rock, old-school downhill and shaped freeride features. Small vertical is offset by technical density and a long operating season.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The chairlift carries bikes; check Caldirola Bike for current tickets and opening days.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 March; closed from 01 December (typical weekend season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; the park operates on selected days.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Genoa</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>Milan</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.seggioviacaldirola.it/caldirock-bike-park/">Seggiovia di Caldirola - Caldirock Bike Park</a>. Check its calendar before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>9.150383,44.728194,999</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>caldirola</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>expert bike-park dh freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>03-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>12-01</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Abetone Gravity Park (Tuscany) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lift-served gravity in the Tuscan Apennines</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A central-Italian reference with downhill race lines, roots, rock, flow and jump features through high beech and conifer forest. It offers beginner progression but is best known for technical expert riding.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer lifts carry bikes; check the park for current passes and open sectors.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 06 June; closed from 04 October (typical weekend/holiday season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; check the operating calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Florence</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr><tr><td>Lucca</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h20</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.abetonegravitypark.it/">Abetone Gravity Park</a>. Verify current operations.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>10.664464,44.144500,1388</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>abetone</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-06</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>10-04</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Cimone Bike Park (Sestola, Emilia-Romagna) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Monte Cimone lift network above Sestola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A broad Apennine destination mixing lift-served downhill, freeride, enduro and trail riding. Volcanic-looking rock, roots and long forest lines range from smooth flow to technical black descents.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Selected summer lifts carry bikes; check Cimone for the current bike pass and sector schedule.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 13 June; closed from 27 September (typical summer window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; verify open lifts and trails.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Modena</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>Bologna</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.cimone.it/">Cimone Bike Park</a>. Verify current operations.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>10.786868,44.228066,832</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>cimone</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-13</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>09-27</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Ponte di Legno - Tonale Bike Park (Lombardy/Trentino) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>High-alpine lift network from Ponte di Legno toward Tonale</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Long lift-linked descents combine bike-park flow, natural enduro, steep forest and rocky alpine terrain across a large vertical range. Easier family routes coexist with technical lines toward the valley.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer gondolas and chairlifts carry bikes; check Pontedilegno-Tonale for the current bike pass.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 20 June; closed from 20 September (typical lift season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; individual lifts have different calendars.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Brescia</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr><tr><td>Edolo</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.pontedilegnotonale.com/en/">Pontedilegno-Tonale</a>. Verify current MTB lift access.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>10.508662,46.258603,1243</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>ponte-tonale</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-20</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>09-20</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Monte Amiata Freeride (Tuscany) [uplift days]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Volcanic forest gravity on Monte Amiata</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A distinctive central-Italian network on an extinct volcano, with deep beech forest, loam, roots, rock gardens, enduro stages and purpose-built freeride. The best descents are technical and feel unusually alpine for Tuscany.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Organized uplift operates on selected days; otherwise climb by pedal or arrange a local shuttle. Check Amiata Freeride before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 April; closed from 01 December (typical riding and uplift season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00 on uplift days<br/><small>Opening is event/calendar-dependent.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Siena</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>Grosseto</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h20</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.amiataturismo.it/">Amiata Turismo</a>. Confirm uplift and trail access.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-green</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>11.623274,42.887426,1724</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>monte-amiata</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>expert natural dh enduro freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>04-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>12-01</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Roccaraso Bike Park (Abruzzo) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lift-served gravity in the central Apennines</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One of southern-central Italy's most relevant lift parks, with downhill, freeride and enduro over open mountain terrain and wooded lower slopes. It covers progression flow through technical rock, roots and jump lines.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Selected summer ski lifts carry bikes; check the operator for current tickets and sectors.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 27 June; closed from 06 September (typical main season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated standard hours; verify open days and lift status.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Naples</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr><tr><td>Rome</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://roccaraso.net/">Consorzio Skipass Alto Sangro</a> and <a href="https://www.roccarasoturismo.it/en/">Roccaraso Turismo</a>. Verify current summer bike operations.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>14.078257,41.850261,1235</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>roccaraso</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-27</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>09-06</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Les Orres Bike Park (Hautes-Alpes) [28 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Three chairlifts above Les Orres 1650 and 1800</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One of France's original purpose-built bike parks, with a broad progression from family flow to World Cup-level downhill, rough roots, steep natural lines and major freeride features. The long vertical and famously shaped tracks make it a national gravity destination.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Prelongis, Pic Vert and Pousterle chairlifts serve the park. Adult day pass 28 EUR at the published 2026 opening tariff.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 13 June; closed from 14 September (published 2026 main season plus September weekends).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Published standard hours; lift availability varies by period and weather.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Gap</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr><tr><td>Embrun</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.lesorres.com/espace-presse/saison-d-ete-2026-c-est-parti">Les Orres 2026 season</a> and <a href="https://www.lesorres.com/activites-et-animations/programme-des-animations/opening-les-orres-bike-park">opening information</a>. Verify live lift and trail status.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.551031,44.514002,1457</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>les-orres</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-13</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>09-14</value></Data><Data name="price_day"><value>28 EUR</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Pra Loup Bike Park (Ubaye) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Telemix de la Clappe above Pra Loup 1600</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>An accessible Southern Alps park with maintained downhill lines for progression, families and experienced riders, mixing sunny open slopes with forest singletrack, berms and technical sections.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Telemix de la Clappe carries bikes. Check the resort ticket shop for the current day tariff; rentals and a wash station are available at the base.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 04 July; closed from 31 August (published 2026 dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Published 2026 lift hours; last descent at 17:00.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Barcelonnette</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Gap</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h20</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.praloup.com/en/activities/bike-park-de-pra-loup/">Pra Loup Tourism</a>. Verify ticket and trail status.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.602503,44.370151,1634</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>pra-loup</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>07-04</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>08-31</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Vars - Risoul Foret Blanche 360 (Hautes-Alpes) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Connected Vars and Risoul lift-served MTB domain</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The two resorts joined their networks for 2026 as Foret Blanche 360: 360 km of DH, enduro, cross-country and e-MTB routes. Vars alone offers green-to-black park lines, wooded singletrack, open alpine terrain and a huge 1800 m descent toward Embrun.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer lifts on both sides serve the connected domain. Check Vars/Risoul for the current combined pass.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 04 July; closed from 31 August (published 2026 daily dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical lift hours; verify the connected-domain schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Briancon</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr><tr><td>Embrun</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.vars.com/summer/experiences-to-live/mountain-biking-in-vars/">Vars official tourism</a>. Verify lift and trail status.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.682570,44.569868,1891</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>vars-risoul</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>07-04</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>08-31</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Montgenevre Bike Park (Hautes-Alpes) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lift-served border park at Montgenevre 1860</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A high-altitude park straddling open alpine slopes and larch forest near the Italian border, with green and blue progression, technical red and black downhill, enduro links and a village pump track.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer lifts carry bikes; current tariffs are published by the resort ticket office.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 27 June; closed from 31 August (typical summer window; verify 2026 lift dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical lift hours; check the official operating calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Briancon</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Turin</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://montgenevre.com/ete/bike-park">Montgenevre Bike Park</a>. Verify prices, lift and trail status.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.721800,44.931171,1859</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>montgenevre</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-27</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>08-31</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Meribel Bike Park (3 Vallees) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lift-served park and enduro hub in the central 3 Vallees</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A large network of shaped downhill, jump lines and natural enduro connects Meribel's villages and high lifts. It offers genuine beginner flow alongside steep roots, rocks and long valley descents, with selected links toward Courchevel.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer gondolas and chairlifts carry bikes seven days a week; check the 3 Vallees summer tariff.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 04 July; closed from 30 August (typical main lift season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:30<br/><small>Estimated standard hours; check the lift calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Moutiers</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Chambery</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.meribel.net/en/resort/cyling-experience/">Meribel official tourism</a>. Verify current lifts and trails.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.566606,45.399064,1464</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>meribel</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>07-04</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>08-30</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>La Plagne Bike Park (Tarentaise) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Colorado chairlift sector up to 2300 m</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A high-volume park with green progression, long blue flow, technical reds and blacks, enduro itineraries and descents linking the altitude villages to the valley. The lower maximum altitude helps it open reliably by late June.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer lifts including Colorado serve the park; check La Plagne for the current MTB pass.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 27 June; closed from 30 August (typical main season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated standard hours; verify the published lift calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Aime-la-Plagne</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Albertville</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h05</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://en.la-plagne.com/explore-the-multitude-of-activities-on-offer/dive-into-the-heart-of-summer/biking/bike-park">La Plagne official tourism</a>. Verify lifts and trails.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.704912,45.504299,2076</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>la-plagne</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-27</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>08-30</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Les Saisies Bike Park (Beaufortain) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lift-served Beaufortain park facing Mont Blanc</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>17 marked runs: 3 green (Coyote, Pikachu, Shrek), 7 blue (Cornifle, Droit dans lo Boets, El'fly, Fends la Bise, Lovely Woods, Monchu, Tsapa Secreta), 4 red (Bougnette, Dre dans l'Pentu, Saisissante, Tabasco) and 3 black (Borat, Cuberote, Natur Hell). Around that sit enduro routes, FFC cross-country loops, play zones and a pump track. The mix runs from approachable flow to rooty, steep forest, and the whole thing faces Mont Blanc.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Three lifts in summer: Legette, Chard du Beurre and Bisanne. Legette and Chard du Beurre run daily from 20 June to 6 September, Bisanne daily from 4 July to 28 August. One day pass covers the Les Saisies and Crest-Voland/Cohennoz bike areas together.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 20 June; closed from 7 September (published 2026 lift dates, with a pre-opening weekend on 13-14 June).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-17:00 (Legette); 09:30-16:55 (Chard du Beurre, Bisanne)<br/><small>Published 2026 hours; verify the daily lift schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Albertville</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Annecy</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h20</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://en.lessaisies.com/accessible-mountains-in-summer/mountain-biking-for-all/bike-park-2/">Les Saisies official tourism</a>. Verify current operations.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.539448,45.757330,1637</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>les-saisies</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-15</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>09-15</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>La Rosiere Bike Park (Espace San Bernardo) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sunny border-facing park above the Tarentaise</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Four downhill tracks and six enduro/e-bike routes deliver up to 1200 m of descent, combining shaped park sections, natural singletrack and panoramic traverses toward the Italian border.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer lifts carry bikes; passes are sold at La Rosiere Centre and Les Eucherts.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 27 June; closed from 06 September (typical summer window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:30<br/><small>Estimated standard hours; verify the current lift calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bourg-Saint-Maurice</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.larosiere.net/bike-park/">La Rosiere Tourism</a> and <a href="https://www.larosiere.ski/en/activity/bike-park">Espace San Bernardo</a>. Verify current operations.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.850258,45.626652,1839</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>la-rosiere</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-27</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>09-06</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Val Cenis Bike Park (Haute Maurienne) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lift-served riding above Lanslevillard and Lanslebourg</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A quieter Maurienne alternative with downhill progression, natural enduro, long forest descents and high-alpine views. It suits mixed groups while retaining technical red and black terrain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Selected summer lifts carry bikes; check Val Cenis for the current tariff and operating sectors.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 28 June; closed from 31 August (typical main season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-16:30<br/><small>Estimated standard hours; verify the lift calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Modane</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Chambery</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.valcenis.com/">Val Cenis Tourism</a>. Verify MTB lifts, dates and trail status.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.864983,45.276345,1847</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>val-cenis</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-28</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>08-31</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Le Lioran Bike Park (Cantal) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Volcanic Massif Central gravity park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One of central France's essential lift parks, with long wooded downhill, volcanic rock, roots, flow and enduro links around Plomb du Cantal. Its wet-weather terrain can become seriously technical.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The cable car and selected lifts carry bikes; check Le Lioran for current MTB pricing.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 27 June; closed from 30 August (typical daily lift season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated standard hours; verify the lift calendar and weather.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Aurillac</td><td>Train / car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Clermont-Ferrand</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.lelioran.com/">Le Lioran resort</a>. Verify current bike access and operations.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>2.753321,45.090665,1153</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>le-lioran</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-27</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>08-30</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Super-Besse Bike Park (Massif du Sancy) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lift-served volcanic park below Puy de Sancy</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A compact all-level park with shaped flow, downhill and enduro on open volcanic slopes and lower forest. Weather changes quickly and the harder lines become slick and exposed in rain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer lifts carry bikes; check the Sancy operator for current pricing.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 04 July; closed from 30 August (typical main season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated standard hours; verify weather and lift status.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Clermont-Ferrand</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.sancy.com/">Massif du Sancy Tourism</a>. Verify current bike-park operations.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>2.856158,45.511458,1311</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>super-besse</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>07-04</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>08-30</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Gerardmer Bike Park (Vosges) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lift-served forest gravity above Gerardmer</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A notable Vosges park complementing nearby La Bresse and Lac Blanc, with short repeated downhill laps, roots, rocks, berms and jump features in dense forest. The black terrain is especially technical when wet.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A summer chairlift carries bikes; check the operator for current opening days and pricing.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 May; closed from 02 November (typical weekend/holiday season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-17:00<br/><small>Estimated standard hours; the park is not necessarily open daily.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Epinal</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Colmar</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h05</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://gerardmer-ski.com/">Gerardmer ski area</a>. Verify current summer bike operations before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.907222,48.053056,1011</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>gerardmer</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>05-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>11-02</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Ax 3 Domaines Bike Park (Ariege Pyrenees) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lift-served Pyrenean park above Ax-les-Thermes</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Long mountain descents combine bike-park shaping with natural Pyrenean roots, rock and forest. Green and blue routes support progression while the hard DH and enduro lines use the resort's substantial vertical.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer lifts carry bikes from the Bonascre plateau; check Ax for current tariffs.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 04 July; closed from 30 August (typical main season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated standard hours; verify the published operating calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Toulouse</td><td>Train + gondola / car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr><tr><td>Ax-les-Thermes</td><td>Gondola</td><td>~10 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.ax.ski/">Ax 3 Domaines</a>. Verify summer bike access and lift status.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>1.815209,42.700577,1379</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>ax-3-domaines</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>07-04</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>08-30</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>EVO Bike Park (Digne-les-Bains) [shuttle park]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Purpose-built gravity park in the Alpes-de-Haute-Provence</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Eleven park pistes: 2 blue, 4 red and 4 black, plus one additional line listed by the park. Named lines include Savage Train, Dirty Wave, Slate Line, Jungle Trail, Whip It, North Shore, Chainsaw, Original Gangsta, Double Black Mamba, Griffus Line and Stratos Line. The terrain combines shaped flow, jumps, technical rock, steep race sections and freeride features.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The park operates its own truck-and-trailer shuttle system. The day ticket is 35 EUR. Booking is required; check EVO for current sessions and pricing.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round, subject to booking, weather and maintenance. Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:30; winter uplift typically ends at 17:00.<br/><small>Check the operator calendar before travelling.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Digne-les-Bains</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Marseille</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://evobikepark.com/bike-park/">EVO Bike Park trail list</a> and <a href="https://evobikepark.com/">EVO Bike Park practical information</a>. Book and verify current trail status before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.266533,44.110976,657</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>evo-bike-park</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Orcieres Bike Park (Champsaur) [lift pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>High-alpine park above Orcieres Merlette 1850</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A sunny Southern Alps network with long downhill and enduro routes, open alpine flow, larch forest, technical rock and large vertical toward the Champsaur valley. It caters to beginners but has serious red and black terrain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer gondolas and chairlifts carry bikes; check the resort for the current pass.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 27 June; closed from 30 August (typical main season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated standard hours; verify the lift calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Gap</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.orcieres.com/">Orcieres Tourism</a>. Verify current bike-park operations.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>6.322065,44.696511,1820</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>orcieres</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-27</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>08-30</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Bike Park Ferme Libert (Malmedy, Belgium) [10 EUR / 10 lifts]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Ferme Libert ski tow - gravity riding above Malmedy</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One of the Benelux's most established gravity parks, with several downhill and freeride lines dropping about 110 m over runs 600-900 m long. Expect roots, steep forest sections, jumps and large freeride features; the hill has hosted Belgian downhill races and Fest Series sessions.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The ski tow carries riders and bikes. Ten uplifts cost 10 EUR; downhill-bike and protection rental is available.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 April; closed from 1 December (typical riding window).<br/>Daily opening hours: schedule varies weekly<br/><small>The operator publishes changing opening days and hours; check before travelling.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Liege</td><td>Car</td><td>~55 min</td></tr><tr><td>Malmedy</td><td>Bike / car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.bikepark-fermelibert.com/fr/accueil.htm">Bike Park Ferme Libert</a>. Opening, uplift and trail conditions can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>6.032635,50.446019,459</coordinates></Point>
