  <Placemark>
    <name>Bikepark Spaarnwoude (Netherlands) [free, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Short gravity lines on Spaarnwoude's artificial hill</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Five purpose-built lines range from accessible flow turns to a serious downhill line with drops and gaps reported up to eight metres. The adjacent technical MTB loop adds rocky and rooty practice despite the low elevation.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Free and pedal- or push-accessed; there is no lift. Respect line closures and avoid soft trails after sustained rain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 01 January; closed from 01 January (normally year-round).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Check local maintenance notices and conditions.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Amsterdam</td><td>Train + bike</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Haarlem</td><td>Bike</td><td>~35 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.mtb-spaarnwoude.nl/">MTB Spaarnwoude</a> and the <a href="https://www.mtbroutes.nl/bikepark/bikepark-spaarnwoude">Dutch MTB routes listing</a>. Check current trail status before riding.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>4.670353,52.441126,3</coordinates></Point>
