  <Placemark>
    <name>Myoko Suginohara MTB (Niigata) [gondola, details unverified]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Suginohara gondola - riding on the flank of Mount Myoko</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Green-season riding uses forest and ski-area terrain around the long Suginohara gondola, with gondola-served downhill described by Japan's national tourism guide. Expect natural mountain riding rather than a large, fully signed modern bike park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Suginohara gondola has carried mountain bikes, but a current 2026 MTB operating calendar and tariff could not be confirmed. Contact the resort before making a dedicated trip.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 July; closed from 1 November (estimated summer-to-autumn window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-16:00<br/><small>Season and hours are estimates; confirm bike carriage and current trail access with the operator.</small><br/><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.japan.travel/national-parks/parks/myoko-togakushi-renzan/see-and-do/myoko-suginohara-ski-resort/">Japan National Tourism Organization</a> and <a href="https://www.princehotels.com/">Myoko Suginohara</a>. Operations can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
