  <Placemark>
    <name>Metabief - Mont d'Or (Jura, FR) [26.90 EUR / Magic Pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Metabief 1020 m - valley station of the Morond chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The biggest bike park in the eastern Jura, and the nearest real downhill to Lausanne. Eight marked downhill and enduro runs share about 390 m of vertical off the Morond, roughly 25 km of trail in total: dark spruce forest, roots and off-camber limestone rather than manicured berms, which makes the reds and blacks ride harder than the modest drop suggests. It rides best in the dry.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Morond chairlift carries bikes, usually 9h30 to 17h30. Day pass 26.90 EUR, four consecutive hours 18.90 EUR. Free with the Magic Pass, including access to the Morond chairlift and bike park. The park opens 1 May 2026 on weekends and public holidays, runs daily from 27 June to 30 August, then returns to weekends in September.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 May; closed from 28 September (published 2026 bike-park dates).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-17:30<br/><small>Published operating hours; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Train + bike</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.magicpass.ch/">Magic Pass</a> and the bike-park operator. Prices are 2026 indications &middot; check before you go.</i><br/><br/>
    <b>Rain sensitivity</b><br/><i>Rain-sensitive: dark spruce forest and clay-heavy Jura soil, slow to dry - rides best in the dry.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
