  <Placemark>
    <name>Davos Klosters - Gotschna (Graubunden) [60 CHF]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Klosters 1190 m - valley station of the Gotschnabahn</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Gotschna Freeride is the gravity draw: 5.8 km and 590 m of descent, more than 200 banked turns and thirty-odd tables, built in the spirit of Whistler's A-Line and maintained to the same standard. Across the valley the Jakobshorn holds the Ischalp flow trail, about 7 km for 1000 m of descent, plus a technique trail that works as a genuine first day out.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Gotschnabahn cable car from Klosters at 1190 m. A day pass including bike transport is about 60 CHF; the bike surcharge alone is 15 CHF, and a bike summer season pass is 160 CHF.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 June; closed from 20 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Zurich</td><td>Train</td><td>~2h15</td></tr><tr><td>Chur</td><td>Train</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.davos.ch/">Davos Klosters</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
