  <Placemark>
    <name>Stoos - Fronalpstock (Schwyz) [funicular + chairlift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Stoos 1295 m - valley station of the Fronalpstock chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A car-free resort accessible only by the world's steepest funicular, with a network of SuisseMobile mountain-bike routes in a panorama setting above Lake Lucerne. Trails are natural and shared-use, descending from Fronalpstock and Klingenstock (1900 m) back to the Stoos plateau (1300 m) or all the way to the valley. The riding is scenic XC and enduro rather than built park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Morschach-Stoos cable car or the Schwyz-Stoos funicular (bike surcharge ~5 CHF). From Stoos, chairlifts to Fronalpstock and Klingenstock carry bikes. A combined return from Schwyz is about 44 CHF + bike supplement.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from June; closed from October (estimated summer lift window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; check the Stoos Bahnen summer timetable.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lucerne</td><td>Train + funicular</td><td>~1h</td></tr><tr><td>Zurich</td><td>Train + funicular</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.stoos.ch/de/">Stoos tourist office</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
