  <Placemark>
    <name>Melchsee-Frutt (Obwalden) [gondola]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Stoeckalp 1080 m - valley station of the Melchsee-Frutt gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>High-alpine XC and enduro riding at 1900-2200 m around Lake Melchsee, with panoramic loops and additional chairlift-served descents from Bonistock (2148 m) and Erzegg (2136 m). Trails are natural mountain paths shared with hikers rather than purpose-built bike trails. The altitude, views and clean air make it a proper summer escape from the lowlands.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Stöckalp-Melchsee-Frutt gondola carries bikes to the high plateau. Additional chairlifts (Cheselen, Jäst, Bettenalp, Erzegg, Bonistock) run higher. Confirm the current bike ticket and lift schedule before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from June; closed from mid-October (estimated summer lift window).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; check the Melchsee-Frutt summer timetable.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lucerne</td><td>Car / bus</td><td>~1h</td></tr><tr><td>Stöckalp valley station</td><td>Gondola</td><td>~15 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://frutt.ch/sommer">Melchsee-Frutt</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
