  <Placemark>
    <name>Bromont (Quebec) [70-95 CAD, dynamic]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Bromont 200 m - valley station of the Express du Village</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The busiest bike park in Quebec and one of the longest-running in North America, with a ticket that also opens the neighbouring Parc des Sommets network. Only 340 m of vertical, but the trail count and the night-riding operation mean people ride here all season rather than making a pilgrimage. Flow, jump lines and technical Eastern Townships granite in about equal measure.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Six lifts serve the mountain from the village at 200 m. Adult single-day tickets are dynamically priced between 70 and 95 CAD - the earlier you book, the cheaper - and an unlimited adult season pass is 699 CAD, taxes extra.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 May; closed from 26 October (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Montreal</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr><tr><td>Sherbrooke</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.bromontmontagne.com/en/mountain-biking/">Bromont</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
