  <Placemark>
    <name>Zona Zero Pirineos (Ainsa, ES) [no lift, free trails]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Ainsa 580 m - internationally known natural enduro trail centre</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A vast signed network built around restored historic paths through Sobrarbe's sandstone ridges, badlands, forests and abandoned villages. Routes range from approachable valley loops to long, exposed and highly technical enduro days. This is natural riding rather than a shaped park; carry navigation, water and repair equipment.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The trails themselves are free and normally climbed under pedal power. Commercial shuttles, guides, rentals and route support are available in Ainsa for riders who want uplift or local knowledge.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Normally rideable year-round. Summer heat can be severe and high routes can hold snow in winter, so spring and autumn are the prime seasons.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Huesca</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h20</td></tr><tr><td>Zaragoza</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h10</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://zonazeropirineos.com/en/">official Zona Zero Pirineos site</a>; respect route-specific closures and shared paths.</i>]]></description>
