  <Placemark>
    <name>Baegyangsan MTB Trails (Busan, KR) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Baegyangsan above central Busan - natural urban mountain-bike network</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A dense mix of forest roads and natural singletrack with sustained climbing, rooty enduro descents and steeper downhill options. Local routes cover beginner, intermediate and advanced riding, but these are shared mountain paths rather than signed, bike-only park tracks. Start from the Busan Children's Grand Park side for convenient access.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no mandatory trail fee: pedal the forest-road climbs and connect the natural descents. Yield to walkers, avoid busy hiking periods and respect any temporary closures.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round. Heavy summer rain, typhoons, ice and freeze-thaw conditions can make the steep natural trails unsuitable; avoid riding when the surface is saturated.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Central Busan</td><td>Bike / metro and bike</td><td>~30 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.visitbusan.net/index.do?lang_cd=en&amp;menuCd=DOM_000000302008001000&amp;uc_seq=446">Visit Busan mountain guide</a> and <a href="https://www.busan.go.kr/geopark_en/baegyangsan">Busan Geopark</a>; trails are shared and unsigned for MTB.</i>]]></description>
