  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Mount Maarat / Patiis Trails (Rizal, PH) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mount Maarat above San Mateo - raw local enduro</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A long-established local network of brutally steep climbs and loose, rooty jungle descents, including the notorious Shotgun area. Lines are informal and technical rather than marked park trails, and land access can change.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No formal lift. Pedal, arrange a local pickup, and ride with people who know current entrances and private-land restrictions.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round in principle, but the dry months from November-May are more reliable. Avoid heavy rain and typhoon periods.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Metro Manila</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: Rizal's established Maarat riding area and local trail reports; access is informal and must be confirmed locally.</i><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: rider reports from the Rizal trail community.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
