  <Placemark>
    <name>Lar National Park / Damavand MTB (IR) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lar Valley beneath Mount Damavand - high-altitude expedition MTB</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A serious point-to-point backcountry ride across alpine plateau, riverbeds, dirt tracks and high passes beneath Iran's 5,610 m volcano. Commercial itineraries rate it highly demanding and normally take several days.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Guided trips use support vehicles and camps; permits and protected-area access must be arranged in advance.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from late May through August in a typical year; snow, river levels and conservation closures control access.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Tehran</td><td>Guide vehicle</td><td>~2h to western approach</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://damavand.camp/tours/mountain-biking/5-day-lar-plain-mtb/">Lar Plain MTB itinerary</a> and <a href="https://www.adventureiran.com/mountain-biking-lar-national-park/">Adventure Iran trip report</a>.</i>]]></description>
