  <Placemark>
    <name>Longjing Tea Hills MTB (Hangzhou, CN) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Longjing tea hills west of Hangzhou - shared forest and village riding</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Steep paved lanes, tea-field tracks and forest paths create short urban-edge rides above West Lake. This is a shared landscape, not a sanctioned gravity park: many paths are pedestrian or agricultural, so use only routes where cycling is allowed.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no trail pass. Pedal from the city or use a local cycling guide.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Best in spring and autumn; avoid monsoon rain, extreme summer heat and crowded holiday periods.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Central Hangzhou</td><td>Bike / metro and bike</td><td>~35 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Indicative urban trail-zone pin. Confirm legal cycling routes locally and always yield to walkers and tea workers.</i><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://wgly.hangzhou.gov.cn/en/">Hangzhou tourism</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
