  <Placemark>
    <name>Shenzhen Wutong Mountain MTB Trails (CN) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Technical singletrack on Shenzhen's highest peak</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Mapped mountain-bike lines on Wutong Mountain (944 m) and surrounding hills include graded singletrack from easy blue (Kunpeng Path) to double-black extreme (Extreme Wutong, mtb:scale 6). The Yantian coastal hills add red-grade speed tracks and enduro lines. The Dayun XC loop (2.4 km) near Longgang is the only purpose-built MTB track in the city.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal up or use local shuttle arrangements. Sightseeing gondolas at OCT East and Qiushuishan do not carry bikes.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Best October-April. Summer brings extreme heat (35 C+), monsoon rain and typhoon risk.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Central Shenzhen</td><td>Metro + bike</td><td>~40 min to Wutong trailhead</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Most trails are unofficial and ride at your own risk; Wutong Mountain's main road formally bans cycling. Verify current access and local conditions before riding.</i><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: OpenStreetMap (30+ mtb-tagged ways, ODbL). Trail access and legality can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>114.191,22.565,340</coordinates></Point>
