  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>West Maui Bike Park (Napili, US) [no lift, free]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Community dirt-jump and skills park in Napili</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A five-acre community bike park with progressive dirt-jump lines, pump and skills terrain developed by the Maui Mountain Bike Coalition with input from Cam Zink. It is a compact practice park rather than a mountain descent.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Free pedal access; no lift. Pedal or push back to the start of each line. Pedal bikes only.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; it closes for rain, saturated ground or high winds. <br/>Daily opening hours: 08:00-18:00<br/><small>Published daily hours; weather closures apply.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lahaina</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Kahului</td><td>Car</td><td>~55 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.mauimountainbike.org/westmauibikepark">Maui Mountain Bike Coalition</a>. Check its channels for weather closures.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
