  <Placemark>
    <name>Moorea Pineapple Route / Opunohu (PF) [shared tracks, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Plantation tracks beneath Moorea's volcanic peaks</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Farm roads and mixed natural tracks wind through pineapple plantations in the Opunohu interior, with connections toward Belvedere viewpoints. Expect scenic cross-country and adventure riding rather than a formal bike park or continuous gravity singletrack.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Rent a mountain bike locally and pedal from the coast. Stay on permitted routes, respect plantation work and ask before entering private tracks.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Rideable year-round; May-October is generally drier. Tropical rain can turn clay tracks muddy very quickly.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Tahiti</td><td>Ferry + bike</td><td>~45 min ferry</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://tahititourisme.pf/en-pf/islands-and-archipelagos/the-society-islands/moorea/escape-to-moorea/">Tahiti Tourisme - Moorea</a>.</i>]]></description>
