  <Placemark>
    <name>Trace des Jesuites (Martinique, MQ) [shared rainforest trail, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Technical rainforest singletrack in northern Martinique</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A narrow historic trail crosses dense rainforest with roots, rocks, stream crossings and persistently slippery ground. Martinique Tourism lists it for advanced mountain biking, but it is principally a shared hiking trail rather than a managed MTB route.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Arrange a point-to-point pickup or return by road. Check current bicycle permission and trail condition with local authorities or a guide before riding, then give absolute priority to walkers.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Best attempted in the drier December-May period. Do not ride after heavy rain, during flood risk or when the trail surface would be damaged.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Fort-de-France</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Morne-Rouge</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.martinique.org/en/blog/activities-sports/mountain-biking-martinique">Martinique Tourism MTB guide</a>. Current access must be checked locally.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
