  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Bisdary Downhill Track (Guadeloupe, GP) [no lift, free]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Official short downhill trail above Riviere-Sens</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A blue-marked 500 m descent drops about 70 m through the Bisdary forest to the marina. It shares part of the Tour du Houelmont hiking trail, so control speed and give pedestrians priority. The run is short but is Guadeloupe's clearest officially documented MTB-specific descent.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Free access; no lift. Pedal or arrange your own vehicle return from Riviere-Sens to Rue des Archives in Bisdary. Parking is unsupervised.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Permanent route, best December-May. Avoid riding during heavy rain, storms or when the shared surface is saturated.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Basse-Terre</td><td>Bike / car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Pointe-a-Pitre</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.lesilesdeguadeloupe.com/en/equipement/bisdary-downhill-track-mtb/">Guadeloupe Islands official trail page</a>, including downloadable route guide.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
