  <Placemark>
    <name>Kok-Zhailau MTB (Almaty, KZ) [shared trails, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Alpine plateau and ridge riding directly above Almaty</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Rocky forest tracks climb from the city edge to the Kok-Zhailau plateau around 2,000-2,200 m. Beginner outings turn around on the plateau; experienced riders can continue toward the meteorological station or exposed ridge terrain. These are busy shared mountain trails, not a bike park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal from Prosveshchenets or the Medeu side, or book a local guided e-MTB outing. Give way to hikers and horses, especially on summer weekends.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Best May-October. Snow, spring mud, thunderstorms and national-park closures affect the higher route.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Central Almaty</td><td>Bike / bus + bike</td><td>~30 min to trailhead</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://tours.xbike.kz/en/guide/kok-zhailau">local Kok-Zhailau cycling guide</a>. Confirm permitted routes locally.</i>]]></description>
