  <Placemark>
    <name>Manali / Solang Valley MTB (Himachal Pradesh, IN) [shuttle, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>India's best-known Himalayan gravity base</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Steep pine-forest singletrack, village paths and rough alpine tracks descend around Solang, Old Manali and the surrounding Kullu mountains. Terrain ranges from guided cross-country to technical enduro and downhill; it is a developing regional network rather than a signed bike park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No verified public bike lift. Local operators arrange 4x4 shuttles, guiding and occasional specialist helibiking, all of which must be booked and checked independently. The government has also planned dedicated Manali and Solang cycling trails, but completion status varies.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Best April-June and September-November. Monsoon rain, winter snow, landslides and heavy Solang road traffic can prevent riding.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Manali</td><td>Bike / shuttle</td><td>~35 min to Solang</td></tr><tr><td>Kullu airport</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://himachaltourism.gov.in/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/8.-DDR-of-Mountain-Biking-Trails-and-EV-HoHo-Buses-F.pdf">Himachal Pradesh mountain-bike trail planning document</a>. Use a current local MTB operator.</i>]]></description>
