  <Placemark>
    <name>Temi / South Sikkim MTB (IN) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Eastern Himalayan riding through tea, forest and mountain villages</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Temi and Ravangla area provides steep jeep tracks, tea-garden lanes, forest paths and long mountain-road links beneath views toward Kanchenjunga. Sikkim promotes multiple mountain-bike routes and a state MTB tour, but this remains guided regional riding rather than a formal trail centre.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Arrange rental, permits, guiding and vehicle support in Gangtok or through Sikkim Tourism. Do not enter tea estates, protected forests or village land without permission.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Best October-May, with the clearest conditions in autumn and spring. Avoid the June-September monsoon because landslides and saturated trails are common.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Gangtok</td><td>Guide vehicle</td><td>~2h30</td></tr><tr><td>Bagdogra airport</td><td>Car</td><td>~4h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.sikkimtourism.gov.in/">Government of Sikkim adventure tourism</a>.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
