  <Placemark>
    <name>Darjeeling / Senchal MTB (West Bengal, IN) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Tea-hill and forest descents beneath Kanchenjunga views</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Steep estate roads, rocky village tracks and forest routes around Darjeeling, Senchal and Tiger Hill create short technical descents and longer cross-country days. Many attractive paths are hiking trails, protected forest or private tea-estate land, so legal route selection matters.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Use a local cycling guide and vehicle drop where permitted. The Rangeet Valley cable car is a sightseeing installation and should not be assumed to carry mountain bikes.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Best October-May. Monsoon rain from June-September brings deep mud, poor visibility and landslide risk.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Darjeeling</td><td>Bike / guide vehicle</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Bagdogra airport</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Regional riding pin based around Senchal. See <a href="https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/west-bengal/darjeeling">Incredible India - Darjeeling</a> and verify every off-road section locally.</i>]]></description>
