  <Placemark>
    <name>Da Lat Pine Forest MTB (Vietnam) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Vietnam's cool-climate pine-forest riding hub</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Dirt roads and natural trails north of Da Lat cross the Langbiang Plateau through pine forest, farms and rolling highland terrain. Routes can be linked into technical singletrack and longer cross-country days, but there is no signed gravity bike park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Rent locally or book a guide and vehicle transfer from Da Lat. Bidoup-Nui Ba and other protected areas require adherence to park access rules.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Best December-April in the drier season. May-November rain makes red dirt and roots slippery, although guided rides operate year-round when conditions permit.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Da Lat centre</td><td>Bike / shuttle</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Da Lat airport</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://vietnam.travel/things-to-do/8-things-to-do-in-dalat">Vietnam Tourism</a>, which recommends mountain biking the pine-forest dirt trails north of the city.</i>]]></description>
