  <Placemark>
    <name>Alyeska Bike Park - Girdwood (Alaska) [35 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Alyeska base 83 m - valley station of the Bear Cub Quad, Girdwood, Alaska</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Alaska's only lift-accessed downhill park, and the setting does most of the work: a base at 83 m with the Chugach rising straight out of Turnagain Arm. The terrain mixes road, singletrack and built features and leans intermediate to advanced, though there is terrain across the ability range.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Bikes load onto the Bear Cub Quad and Ted's Express. A 35 USD all-day lift fee. The resort rents downhill, all-mountain, enduro and full-suspension e-bikes along with protective gear.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Early June to early September, Friday to Sunday 12:00-18:00.<br/>Daily opening hours: 12:00-18:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Girdwood</td><td>Walk / bike</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Anchorage</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.alyeskaresort.com/alyeska-bike-park/">Alyeska Resort - bike park</a> and <a href="https://girdwood.com/information/downhill-biking/">Girdwood - downhill biking</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
