  <Placemark>
    <name>Mammoth Mountain Bike Park (California) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Main Lodge 2684 m - valley station of the Panorama Gondola, Mammoth Mountain, California</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>More than 80 miles of lift-accessed singletrack, over 100 miles counting the cross-country network, and a 3000 ft vertical drop from an 11,053 ft summit - one of the largest and longest-established bike parks in the United States. Kamikaze is the historic one, three and a half miles of dirt service road where racers have hit 60 mph and where the sport's early downhill races were run; Bullet and Chain Smoke are the other expert lines. The volcanic pumice surface is distinctive and rides unlike anywhere else.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Panorama Gondola carries riders and bikes to the summit, with chairlifts serving the lower mountain. Bike-park tickets are sold on the resort's bike park page.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly mid-June to late September. The Kamikaze Bike Games run in September.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Mammoth Lakes</td><td>Car / free town trolley</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Reno</td><td>Car</td><td>~3 h</td></tr><tr><td>Los Angeles</td><td>Car</td><td>~5 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.mammothmountain.com/things-to-do/activities/bike-park">Mammoth Mountain Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://www.mammothmountain.com/things-to-do/activities/bike-park/bike-park-tickets">Mammoth Bike Park - tickets</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
