  <Placemark>
    <name>Woodward Tahoe at Boreal (California) [25 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Boreal base 2185 m - valley station of the Woodward Tahoe bike park lift, Soda Springs, California</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Slabs are the lift-served part - five trails across the ability range on Boreal's front side - with The Trenches alongside as a dirt playground for learning tricks, and an indoor pump track and full Woodward action-sports campus behind it. Small in scale and built for progression rather than vertical.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The chairlift runs 10:00-18:00. Bike park access 25 USD a person. Woodward also runs mountain-bike camps here through the summer.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Daily from mid-August to Labor Day, then Friday to Sunday into early October, with earlier summer operation alongside the camp programme.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-18:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Truckee</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Reno</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr><tr><td>Sacramento</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.rideboreal.com/explore/facilities/our-parks/">Boreal Mountain and Woodward Tahoe - parks and trails</a> and <a href="https://www.rideboreal.com/explore/who-we-are/woodward-tahoe/">Woodward Tahoe</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
