  <Placemark>
    <name>Beaver Creek Bike Park (Colorado) [63 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Beaver Creek Village 2474 m - valley station of the Centennial Express, Colorado</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A quieter, smaller operation than Vail over the hill, because only one lift carries bikes. Around 2000 ft of lift-served vertical, with two advanced descents and a good spread of easier trails - though many of the easier ones are multi-use, so expect walkers and ride accordingly. Spruce Saddle Lodge at the top has food and toilets.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Centennial Express from Beaver Creek Village up to Spruce Saddle. Day pass around 63 USD, week pass around 177 USD. Full and half-day rentals available at the base for trail bikes, cruisers and e-bikes.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly mid-June to the end of September.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Avon</td><td>Car / free shuttle</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Vail</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Denver</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h 15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.beavercreek.com/explore-the-resort/activities/summer-activities/bike-haul.aspx">Beaver Creek - bike haul</a> and <a href="https://www.vailmag.com/travel-and-outdoors/2021/06/mountain-biking-at-beaver-creek">Vail-Beaver Creek Magazine - biking at Beaver Creek</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
