  <Placemark>
    <name>Copper Mountain Bike Park (Colorado) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Center Village 2962 m - valley station of the American Eagle lift, Copper Mountain, Colorado</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Lift-served singletrack off the American Eagle across the full range of grades. The green trails - Lower Enchanted Forest, Easy Feelin' - are genuinely mellow flow rather than fire road, the blues like Collage and Coppertone add jumps, berms and some technical features, and the black lines bring steep descents, large jumps, drops and rock gardens. A high base at 9712 ft means the riding stays cool in midsummer.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The American Eagle chairlift carries bikes. Copper publishes summer lift rates separately from its winter pricing; check before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Late June to early September.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Frisco</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Denver</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.coppercolorado.com/events-activities/summer-activities/mountain-biking/">Copper Mountain - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://www.summitdaily.com/news/bike-guide-copper-mountain-resort/">Summit Daily - Copper Mountain bike guide</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
