  <Placemark>
    <name>Evolution Bike Park - Crested Butte (Colorado) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Crested Butte base 2783 m - valley station of the Evolution Bike Park lift, Colorado</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>27 trails and more than 30 miles of purpose-built singletrack, in a place that was already a legendary cross-country destination before the downhill park was cut. The alpine setting is a large part of the appeal - the views from the top are as good as the riding.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>All lift-served trails start from the top of the Red Lady Express chairlift. The Silver Queen Express also runs in summer but is for scenic rides and walkers only. Check the resort's summer tickets page for the current bike-park rate.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Seven days a week from early June to Labor Day, then weekends only through September. Lifts usually 09:00-17:00.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Crested Butte town</td><td>Car / free shuttle</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Gunnison</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Denver</td><td>Car</td><td>~4 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.skicb.com/travel-guide/crested-butte-mountain-biking.aspx">Crested Butte Mountain Resort - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://gunnisoncrestedbutte.com/blog/crested-butte-mountain-bike-park-trails/">Gunnison-Crested Butte - bike park trails</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
