  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Granby Ranch Bike Park (Colorado) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Granby Ranch base 2539 m - valley station of the Conquest lift, Colorado</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A small, unpretentious hill with a full set of lift-served downhill trails alongside cross-country riding, and the trail building is better than the size of the place suggests: jumps, bermed corners, rock gardens and wooden structures across the intermediate-to-expert range. A useful alternative when Winter Park down the road is busy.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Conquest chairlift carries bikes. Day tickets have historically been among the cheapest lift-served riding in Colorado, but rates change - check the resort's summer tickets page.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Late May to September. Chairlift Wednesday to Saturday 10:00-17:00, Sunday 10:00-16:00.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Granby</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Winter Park</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Denver</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://granbyranch.com/summer-tickets-passes/">Granby Ranch - summer tickets and passes</a> and <a href="https://www.destinationgranby.com/things-to-do/outdoor-and-recreation/biking/">Destination Granby - biking</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
