  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Keystone Bike Park (Colorado) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>River Run base 2832 m - valley station of the Keystone Bike Park gondola, Colorado</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One of the largest lift-served networks in the country: 55 miles of trail and 2360 ft of vertical, from a base at 9280 ft up to Dercum Summit at 11,640 ft. The spread of difficulty is unusually wide - beginners and intermediates get long roller-coaster runs over bridges and berms, while the expert side has rock gardens, rock drops and sustained high-speed terrain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The River Run Gondola, eight to a cabin, carries riders and bikes from 9280 ft to 11,640 ft. Bike-park tickets are sold separately from the scenic gondola fare; check the current rate before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly late June to early September, with the gondola running daily through the summer.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Keystone / Dillon</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Denver</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.keystoneresort.com/explore-the-resort/activities-and-events/summer-activities/mountain-biking.aspx">Keystone Resort - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://news.vailresorts.com/KeystoneSummer25">Keystone summer tip sheet</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
