  <Placemark>
    <name>Telluride Bike Park (Colorado) [closed 2026 - lift works]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Telluride gondola base 2666 m - town-side access to the Telluride Bike Park, Colorado</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/><b>The bike park is closed for the summer of 2026 while Lift 4 is replaced.</b> Cross-country trail access is free during the works, and the gondola still runs. In a normal season the park is gravity-fed with little or no pedalling, its freeride trails reserved for downhill riders only, served by Chair 4 and the gondola.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The free gondola between Telluride and Mountain Village runs 06:30 to midnight, seven days a week, from late May to late October - a 12-minute ride and free even with a bike. Bike-park passes, when the park is running, have been around 50-55 USD a day and 325 USD for the season.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Normally late June to early September daily, then weekends into late September. <b>Not operating in 2026.</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Telluride town</td><td>Walk / free gondola</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Montrose</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 20</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://tellurideskiresort.com/bike-park/">Telluride Ski Resort - bike park</a> and <a href="https://www.telluride.com/discover/the-gondola/">Visit Telluride - the gondola</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
