  <Placemark>
    <name>Powderhorn Bike Park (Colorado) [49-54 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Powderhorn base 2502 m - valley station of the Flat Top Flyer, Grand Mesa, Colorado</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>15 miles of purpose-built trail on 1650 ft of vertical, on the flank of the Grand Mesa above Grand Junction. Sweeping switchbacks, banked turns and long fast straightaways are the house style. Mutton Buster is the beginner descent and is genuinely rideable by anyone who can work the brakes; Pinball is the other end - steep, rocky and hard on suspension.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Flat Top Flyer high-speed quad. Day pass 49 USD on Thursdays, 54 USD Friday to Sunday, and 29 USD for anyone renting a bike. Season pass around 239 USD.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The summer season, roughly June to September.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Grand Junction</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Palisade</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.powderhorn.com/plan-purchase/bike/bike-park-tickets-passes.html">Powderhorn - bike park tickets and passes</a> and <a href="https://powderhorn.com/plan-purchase/bike/bike-trails.html">Powderhorn - bike trail report</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
