  <Placemark>
    <name>Jarrod's Place Bike Park (Georgia) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Jarrod's Place - shuttle-served bike park, Summerville, Georgia</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Georgia's first shuttle-served bike park, laid out like a ski mountain with green, blue, black and double-black grading. The mix covers enduro singletrack, flow lines, an A-Line style jump trail and a skills and beginner area, with both shuttle and pedal-accessible trails.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift - shuttle.</b> A truck and trailer runs riders to a drop-off near the top, 10:00-17:00 Thursday to Sunday. Park headquarters has toilets, showers, a bike wash and a full-service mechanic; rentals, camping and private lessons available.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Thursday to Sunday 09:00-18:00, open rain or shine.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-18:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Summerville</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Chattanooga</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr><tr><td>Atlanta</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://jarrodsplacebikepark.com/">Jarrod's Place Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://jarrodsplacebikepark.com/pages/park-info">Jarrod's Place - park info</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
