  <Placemark>
    <name>Brundage Bike Park - McCall (Idaho) [25 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Brundage base 1783 m - valley station of the Bluebird Express, McCall, Idaho</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Over 30 miles of lift-served downhill and multi-directional cross-country trail. Elk Trail is the signature - six miles of old-school flow, more ride than descent. Hidden Valley is the aggressive counterpart, dropping 1600 ft through fast chutes, big jumps, tight corners, drops and log rides. Lakeview and Rock Garden fill in between, and a trail now connects the resort to Bear Basin.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Bluebird Express to the summit. All-day lift pass 25 USD - among the best value lift-served riding in the west. Cross-country trails are free and open seven days a week. Kona and Rossignol rentals, restaurant, free disc golf and a small campground on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>From Father's Day weekend, Wednesday to Sunday 10:00-16:30.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:30<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>McCall</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Boise</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h 15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://brundage.com/mountain-biking/">Brundage Mountain Resort - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://bermstyle.com/brundage-bike-park-mccall-idaho/">Bermstyle - Brundage Bike Park</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
