  <Placemark>
    <name>Silver Mountain Bike Park - Kellogg (Idaho) [50 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Kellogg gondola base 697 m - valley station of the Silver Mountain gondola, Idaho</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>40 gravity trails, and the approach is unlike anywhere else in the country: the gondola starts in the town of Kellogg right off Interstate 90 and climbs 3.1 miles - the longest single-stage gondola in North America - to the top of the park in twenty minutes, with no mountain road to drive. The descents are long, with an average trail taking 45 minutes to an hour. The Chair 3 zone gives 800 vertical feet of shorter, less committing trail for riders finding their feet. Voted the Northwest's best bike park four years running.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The gondola from Kellogg plus chairlifts on the mountain. Day tickets 50 USD. Ride and Dine tickets on summer Fridays add a mountain-top barbecue and live music.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly mid-June to late September.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Kellogg</td><td>Walk to the gondola</td><td>In town</td></tr><tr><td>Coeur d'Alene</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Spokane</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.silvermt.com/index.php/mountain/bike-park">Silver Mountain - bike park</a> and <a href="https://www.silvermt.com/index.php/tickets/bike-park-lift-tickets">Silver Mountain - bike park lift tickets</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
