  <Placemark>
    <name>Bald Mountain Bike Park - Sun Valley (Idaho) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>River Run Plaza 1755 m - valley station of the Sun Valley gondola, Ketchum, Idaho</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Over 3100 vertical feet of lift-accessed trail, including what Sun Valley bills as the longest purpose-built downhill trail in the United States. Warm Springs is the one that gets talked about - nine miles descending 2500 ft. River Run, Mindbender and Pale Rider are the other main lines. Bald Mountain is a big, open, sagebrush-and-fir hill and the descents feel like it.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Lift-served access is only from River Run Plaza, where the gondola takes bikes 2000 vertical feet in eight minutes. Wednesday to Sunday, 09:00-16:00.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Trails open once the snow melts and the surface dries, typically from late spring, through to autumn.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-16:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Ketchum</td><td>Car / bike</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Boise</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h 45</td></tr><tr><td>Twin Falls</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.sunvalley.com/things-to-do/biking/">Sun Valley - biking</a> and <a href="https://visitsunvalley.com/to-do/bald-mountain-summer-lift-access/">Visit Sun Valley - Bald Mountain summer lift access</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
