  <Placemark>
    <name>Mt. Abram Bike Park (Maine) [42 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mt. Abram base 514 m - the bike park base, Greenwood, Maine</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>8.5 miles of downhill across about 14 trail segments on 1000 ft of vertical, and a well-earned reputation for what a small hometown ski area can build. The West Side chair serves most of the park and holds the beginner flow and progression terrain; the Main Side lift reaches the summit trails, which include some of the most technical double blacks on the East Coast alongside jump lines.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Two fixed-grip chairlifts, run slower in summer with staff loading the bikes. Lift tickets 42 USD. The West Side lift runs all open days, the Main Side lift Friday to Sunday.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Thursday to Sunday from mid-June through the summer.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bethel</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Portland</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://mtabram.com/bike-park/trail-map/">Mt. Abram Bike Park - trail map</a> and <a href="https://www.singletracks.com/mtb-trails/mt-abram-bike-park-in-maine-has-redefined-what-a-hometown-ski-area-can-build-for-mountain-bikers/">Singletracks - Mt. Abram Bike Park</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
