  <Placemark>
    <name>Thunder Mountain Bike Park - Berkshire East (Massachusetts) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Berkshire East 178 m - valley station of the Thunder Mountain Bike Park lift, Charlemont, Massachusetts</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>10 miles of lift-served trail built by Highland's crew and widely rated the best purpose-built park in southern New England. The range runs from introductory greens to expert jump and technical lines, with Sugar Line the long one at 3.3 miles and The Gronk, Juggernaut and Schist covering the harder end.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A chairlift serves the park. Rentals, lessons and a full retail shop on site. The season pass includes two lift tickets each to Burke Mountain and Killington plus 50 percent off further Burke tickets.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Late spring to mid-autumn.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Charlemont</td><td>Car</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Greenfield</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Boston</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h 15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://berkshireeast.com/summer/thunder-mountain-bike-park/tickets-passes">Berkshire East - Thunder Mountain tickets and passes</a> and <a href="https://mtbparks.com/Massachusetts/298-Thunder-Mountain-Bike-Park-Berkshire-East/View-details.html">MTB Parks - Thunder Mountain Bike Park</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
