  <Placemark>
    <name>The Highlands Bike Park - Harbor Springs (Michigan) [from 35 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>The Highlands base 242 m - valley station of the Camelot 6, Harbor Springs, Michigan</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>22 miles of lift-served trail and the only lift-served bike park in Michigan proper: three greens, six blues, four blacks, two double blacks and one line the resort describes as for professionals only. Designated uphill routes run alongside the lift. The Camelot 6, opened in 2023, is a six-seat bubble chair - the fastest lift in the Midwest.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Camelot 6 carries bikes. Day passes from 35 USD.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Late spring to mid-autumn.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Harbor Springs</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Petoskey</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Traverse City</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.highlandsharborsprings.com/activities/bike">The Highlands Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://petoskeyarea.com/places/the-highlands-bike-park/">Petoskey Area - The Highlands Bike Park</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
