  <Placemark>
    <name>Marquette Mountain Bike Park (Michigan) [closed - lift works]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Marquette Mountain base 236 m - valley station of the bike-park chairlift, Michigan</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/><b>The bike park is closed to the general public this summer while a new chairlift is installed</b>, opening only for three scheduled race events. In a normal season it is 10 trails from beginner to expert on 600 ft of vertical: Snake Oil, Easy Rider and Weasel Connector are the smooth ones, The Original DH adds tight corners and jumps, and the expert terrain is rocky and technical. The wider Marquette area holds some of the best singletrack in the Midwest and is unaffected.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A chairlift normally serves the park, Fridays (selected), Saturdays and Sundays. A season pass without lift access is 50 USD. Everyone using the property needs a pass and a signed waiver.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/><b>Closed to the public for the current summer - check the operator before travelling.</b> Normally summer through early autumn.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Marquette</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Green Bay</td><td>Car</td><td>~3 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.marquettemountain.com/summer/downhill-bike-park/">Marquette Mountain - downhill bike park</a> and <a href="https://www.travelmarquette.com/outdoor-adventure/biking/">Travel Marquette - biking</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
