  <Placemark>
    <name>Detroit Mountain Bike Park (Minnesota) [34 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Detroit Mountain base 439 m - valley station of the Q-Lift, Detroit Lakes, Minnesota</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Eight lift-accessible gravity trails plus 13 miles of cross-country singletrack, on a community-run recreation area rather than a commercial resort. The blue and black lines carry large berms, jumps and drops; the Sasquatch switchback climb is there for anyone who would rather earn the descent than buy a lift ticket.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The chairlift runs at weekends from Memorial Day to Labor Day. A single ride is 11 USD and an all-day pass 34 USD; trail access without the lift is 8 USD.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Late May to early September for lift-served riding; cross-country trails run longer.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Detroit Lakes</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Fargo</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://detroitmountain.com/mountain-biking/">Detroit Mountain - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://detroitmountain.com/summer-pricing-hours/">Detroit Mountain - summer rates and hours</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
