  <Placemark>
    <name>Shepherd Mountain Bike Park (Missouri) [free to ride, shuttle extra]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Shepherd Mountain - shuttle base, Ironton, Missouri</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Over 10 miles of purpose-built downhill on 600 ft of vertical in the Arcadia Valley - one green, two blue and two black gravity trails, covering beginner to pro. The Midwest has very little of this, which is why the park drew attention when it opened.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift - shuttle.</b> A shuttle runs to the top seasonally from March to November, with limited space, so tickets should be bought in advance. <b>Riding and hiking are free</b> from sunrise to sunset if you are happy to climb; you only pay for the shuttle.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>March to November for the shuttle; the trails are open year round, weather and conditions permitting.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Ironton</td><td>Car</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>St Louis</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://shepherdmountainbikepark.com/">Shepherd Mountain Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://shepherdmountainbikepark.com/mountain-bike-trails">Shepherd Mountain Bike Park - trails</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
