  <Placemark>
    <name>Big Sky Bike Park (Montana) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mountain Village 2300 m - valley station of Ramcharger 8, Big Sky, Montana</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Over 50 miles of biking trail with 20-plus miles of it lift-served downhill, and essentially the only lift-served riding in Montana at this scale. Three lifts serve distinctly different terrain: the Explorer gondola covers beginner and easy ground, while Ramcharger 8 and Swift Current 6 open the harder trails higher up. Lone Peak above it all makes for a memorable backdrop.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Ramcharger 8, Swift Current 6 and the Explorer Gondola all carry bikes on a single ticket. The Sky Pack gives four days of riding for 119 USD plus 25 percent off additional days; the Gold season pass includes unlimited summer bike access.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Mid-June to mid-September.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Big Sky town</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Bozeman</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr><tr><td>West Yellowstone</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://bigskyresort.com/summer-activities/mountain-biking">Big Sky Resort - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://www.bigskyresort.com/summer-activities/mountain-biking/tickets">Big Sky Resort - mountain biking lift tickets</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
