  <Placemark>
    <name>Whitefish Bike Park (Montana) [62 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Whitefish base 1367 m - valley station of the bike-park chairlifts, Montana</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>More than 23 miles of lift-accessed downhill and cross-country trail dropping over 2300 vertical feet down the face of Big Mountain, split into three progression zones: Bad Rock at the bottom, B-Side in the middle, and the high-altitude Summit Zone. That structure is the point - you can spend a day in one zone and move up when ready. Smooth flowing singletrack with rolling features at one end, big jumps, high-speed berms and technical rocky drop-ins at the other.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Chairlifts from the base village. Adult full-day ticket 62 USD including lift access. The park runs 10:00-17:30 through the summer.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The Bad Rock zone and cross-country trails open from Memorial Day; the full park runs through the summer, snow and weather permitting.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:30<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Whitefish</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Kalispell</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Glacier National Park</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://skiwhitefish.com/mountain-biking/">Whitefish Mountain Resort - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://explorewhitefish.com/entries/mountain-biking-at-whitefish-mountain-resort/39bfed8e-49b8-4b1c-9d9c-0b9270127003">Explore Whitefish - mountain biking at the resort</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
