  <Placemark>
    <name>Loon Mountain Bike Park (New Hampshire) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Loon base 265 m - valley station of the bike-park lift, Lincoln, New Hampshire</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The largest lift-served park in the White Mountains: over 15 miles of downhill terrain and more than 8 miles of cross-country, on 1000 ft of lift-served vertical. Flow, berms, jumps and technical ground, from smooth beginner trails through to rowdy freeride lines, and the layout is built around progression.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Lift access plus the Gondola Skyride, which day tickets include. A Downhill Discovery package bundling a two-hour lift ticket, rental and a lesson starts at 79 USD; free introductory lessons have been offered for riders new to lift-served biking. Friday evenings run late with music and food.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Mid-June to early September.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lincoln</td><td>Car</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Concord</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 15</td></tr><tr><td>Boston</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h 15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.loonmtn.com/summer-activities/biking/bike-park/about-bike-park">Loon Mountain Resort - about the bike park</a> and <a href="https://www.loonmtn.com/lift-tickets/mtb-ticket">Loon Mountain - MTB day tickets</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
