  <Placemark>
    <name>Pajarito Bike Park - Los Alamos (New Mexico) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Pajarito base 2735 m - valley station of the Townsight Quad, Los Alamos, New Mexico</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Over 1200 vertical feet across a 30-trail system built and looked after largely by local volunteers, with dirt trails alongside North Shore style wooden features and a spread from beginner to expert. Small, community-run and genuinely good - a different proposition from Angel Fire two hours north.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Townsight Quad carries bikes. Day tickets are inexpensive; check the current rate with the ski area.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Lifts run Saturdays and Sundays 09:00-15:00 from mid-May to late October.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-15:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Los Alamos</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Santa Fe</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr><tr><td>Albuquerque</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.pajarito.ski/pajarito-mountain-biking/">Pajarito Mountain - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://www.pajarito.ski/">Pajarito Mountain Ski Area</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
