  <Placemark>
    <name>Beech Mountain Bike Park (North Carolina) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Beech Mountain base 1430 m - valley station of the bike-park chairlift, North Carolina</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The first lift-assisted bike park in North Carolina, with the chairlift running to a 5506 ft summit - the highest ski area in the eastern United States. Ten trails from easy through to expert-only: the beginner lines are smooth with manageable features, while the advanced terrain is steep and technical with a lot of rock, tricky corners and wooden descents.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A chairlift to the summit. All riders need a chairlift pass whether or not they hire a bike; one-time and all-day passes are sold at Ski Beech Sports in the resort village, which also rents bikes.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Thursday to Sunday from late May into early autumn.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Banner Elk</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Boone</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Charlotte</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.beechmountainresort.com/summer/mountain-biking/">Beech Mountain Resort - bike park</a> and <a href="https://beechmtn.com/visit/bike-park-beech-mtn-resort/">Beech Mountain Visitor Center - bike park</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
