  <Placemark>
    <name>Sugar Mountain Bike Park (North Carolina) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sugar Mountain base 1249 m - valley station of the Summit Express, North Carolina</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One of the newer North Carolina parks and unapologetically old-school in style: what it lacks in jumps it makes up in steep, rocky, technical ground, with tall berms and rollers among the rock. Beginner and intermediate trails sit alongside the signature expert terrain. The summit at 5300 ft keeps summer highs in the 60s and 70s Fahrenheit, which is the other reason to come.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Summit Express chairlift carries riders and walkers to the 5300 ft peak. Summer season pass 350 USD adult and 250 USD for 11 and under, covering unlimited bike park and lift use. Scott Ransom rental 175 USD a full day adult, 150 USD half day. Helmets required, full-face on the expert downhill trails.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Memorial Day weekend, then from the 4th of July weekend through September and into early October in some years.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Banner Elk</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Boone</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Charlotte</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h 15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://skisugar.com/bikepark/">Sugar Mountain Resort - bike park</a> and <a href="https://seesugar.com/summer-bike-lift/">Village of Sugar Mountain - bike park and lift rides</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
