  <Placemark>
    <name>Ride Rock Creek (North Carolina) [50-55 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Ride Rock Creek 721 m - shuttle base, Zirconia, North Carolina</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>300 acres bought and built specifically for downhill riding by the professional downhill racer Neko Mulally, open since 2022. Five downhill-specific trails across a range of levels, mixing natural features with jump lines, and explicitly designed around rider progression rather than raw difficulty. There is nothing else quite like it in the region.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift - shuttle.</b> Buses with custom bike trailers, built by Windrock, run throughout opening hours. Day passes 50-55 USD, monthly from 95 USD, season passes from 449 USD, all including shuttles. On-site shop with rentals, parts, gear, snacks and a full-time mechanic.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Friday to Sunday 10:00-17:00.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Hendersonville</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Asheville</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Greenville, SC</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://riderockcreek.com/">Ride Rock Creek</a> and <a href="https://riderockcreek.com/our-story/">Ride Rock Creek - our story</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
