  <Placemark>
    <name>Horns Hill Bike Park (Ohio) [free, shuttles vary]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Horns Hill Park 291 m - shuttle and access road, Newark, Ohio</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A city park that has become the best mix of everything mountain biking offers in Ohio: jumps, drops, rocks, roots, downhill and flow trails, steep tech, jump lines including pro-level ones, big drops, and some genuinely hard climbing. The front-side downhill trails drop off the park road at the top of the hill and are intermediate to very advanced - short runs of one to two minutes down the west side.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift.</b> The park road reaches the top, and organised shuttles for the front-side downhill trails run many weekends. The very active Horns Hill Facebook group is where shuttle schedules get posted; the trails themselves are free public park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The riding season, roughly spring to late autumn.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Newark</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Columbus</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.combomtb.com/races/horns-chill-downhill">COMBO - Horns cHill Downhill</a> and <a href="https://www.singletracks.com/bike-trails/horns-hill-park/">Singletracks - Horns Hill Park</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
