  <Placemark>
    <name>Spider Mountain Bike Park (Texas) [21-59 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Spider Mountain 329 m - valley station of the Texas Eagle lift, Burnet, Texas</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The only lift-served mountain biking in Texas, and the only lift-served bike park in the United States open year round. A repurposed ski lift carries riders 350 ft to the summit above Lake Buchanan, where 18 downhill trails from green to double black are cut into limestone. The vertical is small; the surface and the year-round season are what make it worth the trip.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Texas Eagle chairlift. Tickets from 21 USD bought in advance online, typically 25-49 USD depending on demand, and a flat 59 USD walking in. A 12-month unlimited pass is also sold.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year round - the only US bike park that can say it.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Burnet</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Austin</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.spidermountain.com/">Spider Mountain Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://www.tourtexas.com/attractions/spider-mountain-bike-park-hours-prices-bike-rentals">Tour Texas - Spider Mountain hours, prices and rentals</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
