  <Placemark>
    <name>Brian Head Bike Park (Utah) [from 14 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Brian Head base 2927 m - valley station of the Giant Steps Express, Utah</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>19 lift-served trails at the highest base elevation of any resort in Utah, from the beginner flow of Color Flow up to Timberline, which is rowdy and advanced, and the double blacks Lil' Gritty and Wildflower. The lift also opens the door to a very large network beyond the resort boundary, including the 190-mile Aquarius Trail hut system - so it works as a base for backcountry days as well as park laps.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Giant Steps Express, 09:30-17:00. Tickets start around 14 USD on selected dates, and children 12 and under get unlimited free uplift all summer.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Daily from late June to mid-August, then Friday to Sunday from mid-August to late September.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-17:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Cedar City</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Las Vegas</td><td>Car</td><td>~3 h 30</td></tr><tr><td>Salt Lake City</td><td>Car</td><td>~3 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.brianhead.com/mountain-biking/">Brian Head Resort - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://www.visitutah.com/articles/guide-to-brian-head-mountain-biking">Visit Utah - guide to Brian Head mountain biking</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
