  <Placemark>
    <name>Deer Valley Bike Park - Park City (Utah) [12 USD pedal pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Snow Park base 2202 m - valley station of the Deer Valley Bike Park lifts, Utah</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Around 60 miles of trail, four of them flow trails built by Gravity Logic, and one of the oldest lift-served parks in the country - Deer Valley was hauling bikes when very few American resorts did. The full system is open again after several seasons of partial closures for construction. Cross-country trails here are multi-use and multi-directional.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Three chairlifts carry bikes: Silver Lake Express from the base, and Sterling Express and Homestake Express mid-mountain. A Pedal Pass at 12 USD a day or 50 USD for the season covers riders who pedal up rather than buy lift access; a lift ticket or season pass is what you need to download. Multi-use cross-country trails stay free.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Mid-June to the end of September.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Park City</td><td>Car / free bus</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Salt Lake City</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.deervalley.com/things-to-do/activities/mountain-biking">Deer Valley Resort - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://www.deervalley.com/plan-your-trip/tickets-and-passes">Deer Valley Resort - tickets and passes</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
