  <Placemark>
    <name>Sundance Bike Park (Utah) [65 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Ray's base 1915 m - valley station of Ray's lift, Sundance, Utah</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>25 miles of lift-served trail on the flank of Mount Timpanogos. Ray's lift gives 1200 vertical feet between Ray's Base and Ray's Summit, with Ray's Run, Scotts Pond and Archies Loop the main descents; stronger riders carry on up to Mandan Summit on the Outlaw Express for steeps, bermed turns, rollers and jumps on a flowing trail system. The setting - Redford's resort, dense aspen and fir under a 3600 m peak - is a large part of why people ride here.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Ray's lift, 100 ft west of the bike shop, and the Outlaw Express. A full day is 65 USD; the summer season pass runs 199 USD early and 250 USD later. Lifts 10:00-17:00 daily.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly May to October.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Provo</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Salt Lake City</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.sundanceresort.com/summer-activities/mountain-bike-lift-rides/">Sundance Mountain Resort - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://www.skiutah.com/blog/authors/lexi/guide-to-mountain-biking-at1/">Ski Utah - guide to mountain biking at Sundance</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
