  <Placemark>
    <name>Woodward Park City [from 53 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Woodward Park City 1967 m - valley station of the Hot Laps lift, Utah</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>An action-sports campus rather than a mountain, and it is built for progression: five flow trails, a BMX dirt-jump zone, a pump track, an airbag zone and dedicated learning areas, with an indoor facility alongside. If you want to learn to jump properly rather than survive a mountain, this is the place in Utah to do it.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Hot Laps lift is fitted with bike carriers. Adult bike-haul passes from 53 USD online, with half and full-day tickets sold ahead; summer season pass 199 USD for ages 4 and up. Lifts from 10:00, last chair 19:45 in the main season.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Daily from late June to early September, then Thursday to Sunday to early October.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-19:45<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Park City</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Salt Lake City</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.woodwardparkcity.com/tickets/bike-park/">Woodward Park City - bike park tickets</a> and <a href="https://www.skiutah.com/blog/authors/tony/woodward-park-city-is-utah-s-newest/">Ski Utah - Woodward Park City lift-served biking</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
