  <Placemark>
    <name>Mount Snow Bike Park (Vermont) [55 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Main base 609 m - valley station of the Canyon Express, Mount Snow, Vermont</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One of the original East Coast downhill mountains, with trails across the full range from smooth beginner routes to technical descents thick with roots, rocks and berms - the classic New England surface, which rewards line choice more than raw speed.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Canyon Express carries bikes; the Bluebird Express runs scenic rides. Day pass 55 USD for unlimited downhill laps on the Canyon Express. Lifts Friday to Sunday 10:00-17:00 through summer and into the foliage season.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Late May through to October, into the autumn colours.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>West Dover</td><td>Car</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Brattleboro</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Boston</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.mountsnow.com/explore-the-resort/activities-and-events/summer-activities/mount-snow-bike-park.aspx">Mount Snow Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://www.mountsnow.com/explore-the-resort/activities-and-events/summer-activities/mount-snow-bike-park/bike-park-passes.aspx">Mount Snow - bike park passes</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
