  <Placemark>
    <name>Western Slope Trails - Massanutten (Virginia) [10 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Massanutten resort access 621 m - west-side entry to the Western Slope trails, Virginia</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>32 miles of pedal trails on the west flank of Massanutten Mountain, and a completely different proposition from the lift-served park on the other side: meandering double-track, machine-built flow and steep technical descents, with the Western Slope Perimeter loop gaining 1600 ft. Built and maintained with the Shenandoah Valley Bicycle Coalition.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift - pedal access.</b> A day pass is 10 USD; an annual pass is 50 USD, or free in exchange for a few hours of trail work.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open daily from January to the start of November, then Sundays only through to early January because of the hunting season.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Harrisonburg</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Charlottesville</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.massresort.com/play/mountain-biking/western-slope/">Massanutten - Western Slope trails</a> and <a href="https://svbcoalition.org/western-slope-trails/">Shenandoah Valley Bicycle Coalition - Western Slope</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
