  <Placemark>
    <name>Stevens Pass Bike Park (Washington) [54 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Stevens Pass 1161 m - valley station of the bike-park chairlift, Washington</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Ten trails and about 11 miles of downhill riding, loaded from the Hogsback Express. The mix is unusually even: green, blue and black natural singletrack alongside machine-cut freeride lines with built features, jumps, wall rides and berms. Jormungandr is the newest addition. The Northwest Cup downhill race returns here each September, which tells you what the steeper end is like.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Hogsback Express. Single-day tickets have been around 54 USD, with an unlimited season pass about 309 USD including friends-and-family tickets. Season pass holders get 25 percent off Whistler Mountain Bike Park day tickets, and Whistler pass holders get 50 percent off here.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Late June to late September.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Leavenworth</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Everett</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 30</td></tr><tr><td>Seattle</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.stevenspass.com/explore-the-resort/activities-and-events/mountain-biking.aspx">Stevens Pass - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://news.vailresorts.com/stevens-pass-2026-summer-tip-sheet">Stevens Pass 2026 summer tip sheet</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
