  <Placemark>
    <name>Snowshoe Bike Park (West Virginia) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Snowshoe Village 1443 m - the bike park base, which sits on the summit, West Virginia</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Nearly 40 downhill trails on 1500 ft of descent plus 100 miles of cross-country - one of the largest trail systems in the East, a certified IMBA Ride Center, and a former UCI World Cup venue. Snowshoe is an inverted resort: the village is on top and you ride down from it. The Basin side holds the beginner and intermediate terrain; the Western Territory is the reason racers come, about 2.4 miles of raw natural ground, rock gardens and sustained steep descent, strictly for advanced and expert riders.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Lifts from the village. Season passes from 289 USD; day tickets sold on the resort's bike park page.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Late May to mid-October.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Marlinton</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Charlottesville</td><td>Car</td><td>~3 h 30</td></tr><tr><td>Washington DC</td><td>Car</td><td>~4 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.snowshoemtn.com/things-to-do/activities/snowshoe-bike-park">Snowshoe Mountain - bike park</a> and <a href="https://ridesnowshoehighlands.com/">Snowshoe Highlands Ride Center</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
