  <Placemark>
    <name>Moab - The Whole Enchilada [commercial shuttle]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Burro Pass trailhead 3220 m - shuttle drop for the Whole Enchilada, Moab, Utah</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>42 km and around 2130 m of descent, strung together from six named trails: over Burro Pass at 3400 m, down through the aspens into Hazard County, along Kokopelli, then Upper and Lower Porcupine Singletrack and finally the Porcupine Rim itself, which drops to the Colorado River. It starts above treeline in alpine terrain and finishes on bare desert rim - very few rides anywhere cover that much ground. The Porcupine Rim section is exposed and consequential, and the descent is long enough that arm and brake fatigue matter more than fitness.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift - commercial shuttle.</b> Several Moab operators run it, among them Whole Enchilada Shuttles, Porcupine Shuttle, Coyote Shuttle, Hazard County Shuttle and Poison Spider Bicycles. Shuttles typically run from March, but the drop at Burro Pass is only added once the snow clears.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The lower sections open from spring, but the full route from Burro Pass usually does not open until after 1 July and runs to October. Shorter versions starting at Hazard County or Kokopelli are used earlier in the season.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Moab</td><td>Car / shuttle up Geyser Pass Road</td><td>~1 h</td></tr><tr><td>Grand Junction</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.mtbproject.com/trail/4670265/the-whole-enchilada">MTB Project - The Whole Enchilada</a>, <a href="https://www.visitutah.com/things-to-do/mountain-biking/mountain-biking-trails/porcupine-rim-and-the-whole-enchilada">Visit Utah - Porcupine Rim and the Whole Enchilada</a> and <a href="https://wholeenchiladashuttles.com/shuttle-info-and-rates/">Whole Enchilada Shuttles - info and rates</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
