  <Placemark>
    <name>Sedona Trail Network [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mescal Trailhead 1370 m - Dry Creek access to the west Sedona trails, Arizona</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Hundreds of kilometres of red-rock singletrack around Sedona, and the surface is what makes it: long stretches of bare slickrock, ledges and chunky sandstone rather than dirt. The west Sedona and Dry Creek cluster reached from here - Mescal, Chuckwagon, Aerie, Canyon of Fools, Ground Control, Deadman's Pass - is the approachable end, mostly intermediate, with Mescal running along the base of Mescal Mountain on slickrock. Chuckwagon is 8.7 km of intermediate riding from the Dry Creek Vista trailhead and links into Mescal, Deadman's Pass and Long Canyon for a figure-of-eight half day. At the other extreme, Hiline is 5 km of expert riding with sustained cliff exposure and consequences for a mistake, usually started from the bottom of Slim Shady in the Village of Oak Creek.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift.</b> The trails themselves are free to ride, but most Coconino National Forest trailheads around Sedona need a Red Rock Pass displayed to park - 5 USD a day, 15 USD a week or 20 USD a year, sold at self-serve stations, visitor centres, local shops and online. A federal interagency pass covers it too. Not every trailhead requires one; check the sign where you park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Spring (March to May) and autumn (September to November) are the seasons. Summer is too hot for anything but dawn starts, and there is no shade on most of it.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Sedona</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Flagstaff</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr><tr><td>Phoenix</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://visitsedona.com/blog/top-10-mountain-bike-trails-in-sedona-arizona/">Visit Sedona - top 10 mountain bike trails</a> and <a href="https://www.sedona.net/mountain-biking">Sedona.net - mountain biking</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
