  <Placemark>
    <name>DuPont State Recreational Forest [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lake Imaging parking area 708 m - main bike staging in DuPont State Recreational Forest, North Carolina</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Around 130 km of singletrack and doubletrack, and the counterpoint to Pisgah half an hour up the road: far more of it is smooth and flowing, which makes it the place riders go when they want to enjoy themselves rather than survive. Ridgeline is the trail DuPont is known for, fast and bermed the whole way down. There is bare granite slickrock to ride as well as dirt, plus waterfalls, lakes and some genuinely technical corners for contrast. Bikes are allowed on nearly all trails here, which is unusual and worth respecting - control your speed, the forest is busy with walkers.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift.</b> Free, and free to park. Lake Imaging, Corn Mill Shoals, Fawn Lake and Guion Farm are the parking areas that work best for riding.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year round.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Brevard</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Hendersonville</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Asheville</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.dupontstaterecreationalforest.com/mountain-biking">DuPont State Recreational Forest - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://www.ncagr.gov/divisions/nc-forest-service/state-forests/dupont-state-recreational-forest/explore-the-forest/biking">NC Forest Service - biking at DuPont</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
