  <Placemark>
    <name>Downieville Downhill (California) [25-40 USD shuttle]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Packer Saddle 2155 m - shuttle drop at the top of the Downieville Downhill, California</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>24 km from Packer Saddle down to Downieville, losing about 1520 m on the classic line and closer to 2070 m on the longer version - one of the defining point-to-point descents in North America and the course of the Downieville Classic. It runs Sunrise into Butcher Ranch, then Third Divide and First Divide to the river. The ground is steep, loose and rocky rather than groomed, and the difficulty is sustained: this is an intermediate-to-advanced ride where the descent lasts long enough that fatigue is the real hazard.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift - commercial shuttle.</b> Shuttles run from Downieville, around 25 to 40 USD a rider depending on the operator, with cheaper repeat runs the same day. Yuba Expeditions is run by the Sierra Buttes Trail Stewardship, the organisation behind most of the trail building and maintenance in the area, so the fare goes back into the trails.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly June to October. Packer Saddle sits at 2155 m and holds snow into early summer, so the full descent opens later than the lower trails.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Downieville</td><td>Car / shuttle up Packer Lake Road</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Truckee</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 30</td></tr><tr><td>Sacramento</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://sierratrails.org/">Sierra Buttes Trail Stewardship</a>, <a href="https://www.downievilleoutfitters.net/">Downieville Outfitters - shuttles</a> and <a href="https://downievilleclassic.com/downieville-classic/downieville-downhill.php">Downieville Classic - the downhill</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
