  <Placemark>
    <name>Oakridge Alpine Trail Network [commercial shuttle]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Top of the Alpine Trail 1131 m - shuttle drop on Road 1910 above Oakridge, Oregon</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Alpine is the trail Oakridge is known for: 21 to 24 km of almost continuous singletrack descent through old-growth Douglas fir to the valley floor. The shuttle route climbs around 465 m to a high point of 1453 m before giving back roughly 1480 m, so it is not a pure gravity run - there is real pedalling in the first half, and Windy Pass around the middle is where the trees open up and the trail cuts along a steep hillside. Kate's Cut-in, a couple of miles down from the northern terminus, is the drop most shuttles use. The wider network around Oakridge and Westfir adds Larison Rock, Larison Creek, Hardesty and the Middle Fork, which between them make the town one of the deepest trail bases in the Pacific Northwest.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift - commercial shuttle.</b> Cog Wild and other local operators run scheduled Oakridge shuttles up North Fork Road and Road 1910. Self-shuttling with two cars is common; the climb up is long.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer and autumn. Snow lingers on the upper trail into June, and the season generally runs until the autumn rains.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Oakridge / Westfir</td><td>Car / shuttle up Road 1910</td><td>~1 h</td></tr><tr><td>Eugene</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.cogwild.com/shuttles/oakridge-mountain-bike-shuttles/">Cog Wild - Oakridge shuttles</a> and <a href="https://www.mtbproject.com/trail/4324612/alpine-3450">MTB Project - Alpine #3450</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
