  <Placemark>
    <name>Copper Harbor Trails (Michigan) [shuttle pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Fanny Hooe Creek trailhead 188 m - village access to the Copper Harbor trails, Michigan</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Around 40 miles of marked and mapped singletrack at the tip of the Keweenaw Peninsula, part of well over 100 miles in the wider area, and an IMBA silver-level Ride Center. The mix runs from gateway and cross-country trails through to proper flow and gravity lines, cut through dense hardwood and cedar with a lot of rock. The descents link the Keweenaw Mountain Lodge, Brockway Mountain and the village, giving runs of nearly 700 ft of vertical over up to three miles - modest numbers by western standards, but the trail quality is why people drive a very long way to get here.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift - shuttle.</b> Keweenaw Adventure Company runs a continuous shuttle between its shop in the village and the top of Brockway Mountain or the Lodge, so the wait is rarely more than 15 minutes. Daily shuttle passes are sold; the trails themselves are free and maintained by the Copper Harbor Trails Club.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Shuttles run daily from Memorial Day weekend through to mid-October. The trails themselves ride from snowmelt to the first snow.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Houghton</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr><tr><td>Marquette</td><td>Car</td><td>~3 h</td></tr><tr><td>Green Bay</td><td>Car</td><td>~5 h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://copperharbortrails.org/">Copper Harbor Trails Club</a> and <a href="https://www.keweenawadventure.com/shuttle-service/michigan-mountain-bike-shuttle/">Keweenaw Adventure Company - shuttle service</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
