  <Placemark>
    <name>Bentonville and Bella Vista Trails [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Slaughter Pen trailhead 393 m - main access to the Bentonville trails, Arkansas</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Over 550 miles of trail across northwest Arkansas, and the most deliberately built riding destination in the United States. Slaughter Pen runs 40-plus miles of singletrack right through Bentonville alongside the paved Razorback Greenway and past the Crystal Bridges museum, and it is built for bikes: drops, jumps, log rides, tabletops, a wall ride and endless berms. Coler Mountain Bike Preserve adds 17 miles of flow with natural drops and jumps for stronger riders, open 05:00 to 22:00. North in Bella Vista, the Back 40 is a 25-mile loop around the east side of town with more of a backcountry feel - long climbs, flowing descents and Ozark rock - and Blowing Springs and Alice in Wonderland link the two systems together with Little Sugar.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift.</b> Everything is free and open to the public. The systems connect by trail and greenway, so you can ride between them rather than drive.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year round. Summer is humid, and the limestone gets slick when wet.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bentonville</td><td>Walk / bike from the square</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>Bella Vista</td><td>Car / trail</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Northwest Arkansas National (XNA)</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.oztrails.com/">OZ Trails Northwest Arkansas</a> and <a href="https://www.visitbentonville.com/sp/bike/">Visit Bentonville - biking</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
