  <Placemark>
    <name>Rosso Cup MTB Course (Lae, Papua New Guinea) [annual event]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lae's large community mountain-bike race</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The annual Rosso Cup combines temporary urban, road and forest race sections around Lae, with hundreds of adult and junior riders. The start, finish and road closures can change by edition; this pin marks the Lae Showground event hub, not a permanent signed gravity trail.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no public bike-park ticket. Participate only through official race registration, or attend as a spectator under the published event access plan.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; This is an event venue, not an independently rideable trail network. Do not follow old race lines through private, urban or forest land without local permission and current safety advice.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The 2026 adult event ran 20-21 June, followed by junior racing the next weekend. There is no public riding season.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lae Nadzab Airport</td><td>Car / taxi</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.thenational.com.pg/bikers-set-for-weekend-tracks/">2026 Rosso Cup report</a> and <a href="https://www.thenational.com.pg/rosso-bike-race-to-hold-finals/">course and Botanical Gardens access report</a>. Use only the organizer's current route and access instructions.</i>]]></description>
