  <Placemark>
    <name>La Thuile Bike Park (Italy) [chairlifts]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>La Thuile: Les Suches gondola valley station (1466 m)</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>La Thuile combines a lift-served park with a huge natural trail area totaling roughly 170 km. Its reputation comes from long, steep and physical enduro stages plus raw downhill tracks with roots, rock, changing lines and serious alpine weather. It has hosted the Enduro World Series and the UCI Downhill and Enduro World Cups.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer chairlifts carry bikes from the Planibel base, with regional summer tickets also connecting other Valle d'Aosta lift areas. Check the current resort tariff because products and included lifts vary by season.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 21 June; closed from 15 September (typical summer indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-17:00<br/><small>Estimated summer lift window; verify published 2026 dates, weather closures and the live trail report.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lausanne</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr><tr><td>Aosta</td><td>Car / bus</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.lathuile.it/index.php/en/natural-trail-area-and-bike-park">official La Thuile bike-park page</a> and <a href="https://balteus.lovevda.it/fr/base-de-donnees/7/vtt/la-thuile/bike-park-la-thuile/2794">Valle d'Aosta tourism</a>. Check current lift dates, tickets and trail status.</i>]]></description>
