  <Placemark>
    <name>Pal Arinsal Bike Park (Andorra) [five lifts]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Pyrenean World Cup gravity above La Massana</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>More than 60 km across roughly 30 circuits with over 1000 m of vertical, including World Cup downhill terrain, technical forest lines, flow, jumps and beginner progression at Bike World. Pal Arinsal is a recurring UCI Mountain Bike World Cup venue and one of southern Europe's benchmark lift-served parks.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Five adapted lifts, including the La Massana gondola, move riders around the park. Half-day through six-day passes are sold online; check the live 2026 tariff because the official page routes prices through its booking system.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 20 June; closed from 13 October (published 2026 dates, with autumn weekends only after 13 September).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-18:00<br/><small>Published peak-season hours; autumn weekends close at 17:00. The park is partially restricted during the 7-12 July 2026 World Cup period.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Andorra la Vella</td><td>Bus / car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Barcelona Airport</td><td>Car / bus</td><td>~3h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.palarinsal.com/en/bike-park">official Pal Arinsal Bike Park page</a> and <a href="https://www.palarinsal.com/fr/station/horaires-ouverture-ete">published 2026 summer hours</a>. Check current lift and race-period access before travelling.</i>]]></description>
