  <Placemark>
    <name>Luang Prabang Jungle MTB (Laos) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Remote jungle singletrack and long natural descents</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The mountains outside Luang Prabang contain steep village tracks, dense-jungle singletrack and rough river-valley links. The one-day Lung Buster route climbs roughly 1100 m before a substantial descent over about 35 km, while multi-day northern itineraries continue through isolated mountain and tribal communities. This is demanding adventure trail riding, not a maintained bike park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift or permanent shuttle. The published guided Lung Buster day starts around 72 USD and includes a bike and helmet; longer supported tours with luggage transport are available. Use a guide because paths are remote, unsigned and pass through communities unfamiliar with independent riders.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 October; closed from 1 May (drier-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>Rainy-season mud, swollen river crossings, heat and limited rescue access make independent riding unsuitable.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Luang Prabang centre</td><td>Guide transfer / bike</td><td>Tour dependent</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://laos-adventures.com/71083">Tiger Trail's Lung Buster MTB route</a> and <a href="https://www.spiceroads.com/tours/northern_laos_mountain_biking">guided Northern Laos singletrack expedition</a>. Book with an established operator and respect village access.</i>]]></description>
