  <Placemark>
    <name>Hilltop Bike Park (Alaska) [chairlift, season pass]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>North America's northernmost lift-served bike park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A compact, professionally built gravity park inside Anchorage with nine trails across 294 vertical feet. Beginner flow progresses toward advanced technical and jump lines, backed by a skills area, pump track and airbag zone. Its modest vertical makes repeated training laps the attraction rather than long alpine descents.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>One triple chairlift carries bikes. The published season pass starts at 300 USD and pedal-only access to trails and airbags starts at 10 USD; current day-ticket pricing should be checked online.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 June; closed from 1 October (typical summer indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: 13:00-20:00<br/><small>Published core bike-park hours; scheduled operating days and special-event hours vary. Complete the current waiver and check trail conditions before arrival.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Downtown Anchorage</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.hilltopskiarea.org/bikepark">official bike-park terrain and lift information</a> and <a href="https://www.hilltopskiarea.org/summer-ticket-info">official tickets, pass and hours page</a>. Check the current calendar and conditions.</i>]]></description>
