  <Placemark>
    <name>Borana / Mount Kenya Enduro (Kenya) [no lift, access by event or guide]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Highland enduro stages beneath Mount Kenya</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The private Borana landscape near Nanyuki has hosted the Mount Kenya 10to4 challenge and documented enduro stages. Expect dry rocky singletrack, fast savanna tracks and rolling descents at altitude. Wildlife and private conservancy management make this an organized-event or guided destination, not a public trailhead.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Race support, pedalling and event vehicles provide access depending on the itinerary. Obtain explicit permission from the conservancy or a current event organizer before bringing a bike.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Never ride independently among wildlife or enter conservancy land without authorization. Follow ranger instructions and use an established local organizer.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 June; closed from 1 November (drier-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: guided access only<br/><small>There is no public operating calendar. Access, wildlife management and rain conditions control whether riding is possible.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Nanyuki</td><td>Authorized vehicle</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: the published record of the Nanyuki enduro and the 10to4 event and <a href="https://www.borana.com/">Borana Conservancy</a>. Confirm a legal guided or event-based visit before travel.</i>]]></description>
