  <Placemark>
    <name>Bakuriani Bike Park (Georgia) [lift access unconfirmed]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Forested downhill trails in Georgia's historic mountain resort</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Bakuriani has designated downhill-only mountain-bike trails on the wooded resort slopes, including the documented N1 line. The lower elevation and forest make it a useful contrast to exposed Gudauri, with natural roots and compact gravity riding around town.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The resort has summer lifts, but current bicycle carriage, park tickets and a dependable 2026 operating calendar were not found. Treat the trails as pedal or locally arranged vehicle access until the operator confirms otherwise.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 June; closed from 1 October (estimated snow-free indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>No verified current bike-park hours. Confirm trail legality, lift carriage and maintenance locally before riding.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Tbilisi</td><td>Car / train and taxi</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://georgia.travel/bike-tour-bakuriani-resort-first-track">Georgia Travel's official Bakuriani bike route</a> and published trail records for the Bakuriani park. Verify current operations locally.</i>]]></description>
