  <Placemark>
    <name>Jebel Sifah MTB Trails (Oman) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Marked coastal-mountain trails southeast of Muscat</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A locally built network around GECO Camp and Jebel Sifah Resort combines graded beginner and intermediate loops, coastal tracks and wadi-side riding. Guided programs can extend into more technical singletrack and enduro-style terrain, making this Oman's clearest organized trail-center offer.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal the loops or book a guided itinerary. Published unguided access with mountain bike, helmet, map and basic mechanical support costs 15 OMR per person per hour; guided rates vary.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 October; closed from 1 May (cooler-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: 07:00-18:00<br/><small>Estimated daylight operation. Extreme heat makes summer riding unsafe; flash floods can affect wadis even when local skies look clear.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Muscat</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://outdoorsoman.com/activitiy/mtb-adventures/">Outdoors Oman's trail-network, rental and guided-tour details</a>. Confirm heat, wadi and trail conditions before departure.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>58.779441,23.431645,5</coordinates></Point>
