  <Placemark>
    <name>Obudu Plateau MTB (Nigeria) [no bike lift documented]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Highland riding on Nigeria's most dramatic plateau</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Obudu Mountain Resort sits around 1600 m in the Sankwala Mountains, surrounded by rolling grassland, deep gorges, forest and steep resort tracks. The resort directory lists mountain biking and hiking trails, but no graded bike-park map or maintained downhill course is published.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A cable car historically climbed about 870 m to the plateau, but current operation and bicycle carriage are not dependable. Treat riding as pedal or locally arranged vehicle access and confirm bike rental, route permission and road conditions directly with the resort.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 November; closed from 1 April (drier-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated resort hours. Heavy rain, fog and poor road conditions can prevent access.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Calabar</td><td>Pre-arranged vehicle</td><td>~6h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.obudumountainresort.com/Obudu%20Mountain%20Resort%20Directory.pdf">official resort directory listing mountain biking</a> and the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Obudu_Plateau">plateau geography and access record</a>. Confirm current operations before travelling.</i>]]></description>
