  <Placemark>
    <name>Dogon Escarpment Cycling (Mali) [do not travel]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Historic expedition riding reference, currently unsafe</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Older supported bicycle itineraries crossed the Dogon Country around the Bandiagara Escarpment using village tracks and mountain bikes, combining rocky plateau edges, sandy approaches and cultural routes. This is retained as a historical map reference, not a currently recommended destination.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. The historical product used guides and village support, but no current safe cycling operation has been verified.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; As of July 2026, official advice is against all travel to Mali due to terrorism, kidnapping, road attacks and unpredictable security. Do not plan or undertake this ride while that warning remains.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 November; closed from 1 March (historical cooler-season indication only).<br/>Daily opening hours: unavailable<br/><small>The date metadata describes climate and does not mean the destination is open or safe.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bamako</td><td>Travel currently advised against</td><td>Unavailable</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.ibike.org/bikeafrica/mali/index.htm">historical Dogon mountain-bike itinerary</a> and the <a href="https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mali">current official warning against all travel</a>.</i>]]></description>
