  <Placemark>
    <name>Kédougou / Dindefelo MTB (Senegal) [guided, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Senegal's rare mountain and waterfall terrain</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Fouta Djallon foothills around Kédougou, Dindefelo and Dandé are Senegal's clearest mountain-bike landscape. Community traces document rides near Étiolo and Dindefelo, while regional tourism sources identify the rough tracks and mountain relief as suitable for VTT. Expect village paths, rock, dust and short natural descents rather than a bike park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift or permanent shuttle. Arrange a local guide and vehicle from Kédougou, and obtain community or reserve permission for the exact route.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; Do not ride protected chimpanzee habitat or hiking-only waterfall paths without authorization. Heat, remoteness and seasonal water require conservative planning.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 November; closed from 1 June (drier-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: guided daylight access only<br/><small>No formal MTB operating calendar exists.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Kédougou</td><td>Guide vehicle</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.au-senegal.com/kedougou-terre-d-aventure-et-de-decouvertes%2C18265.html">regional VTT terrain overview</a> and the <a href="https://www.wikiloc.com/trails/mountain-biking/senegal/kedougou">documented Kédougou MTB traces</a>. Confirm the route with a local guide.</i>]]></description>
