  <Placemark>
    <name>Abaga Forest MTB Loop (Gabon) [community route, no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Recorded tropical-forest riding north of Libreville</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A community-recorded 17.6 km mountain-bike loop around Abaga gains about 263 m beside the Ikoï Mondah forest landscape. Expect humid dirt roads and informal forest tracks rather than signed gravity trails; the available recording does not document grading, maintenance or a dedicated trail organization.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift, shuttle or formal admission is documented. Pedal the loop with a local rider and verify land access before leaving public roads.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; The nearby Ikoï Mondah forest is protected. A community GPS trace is not proof that every segment remains legal: respect closures, avoid sensitive forest and do not ride after heavy rain.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 June; closed from 1 October (relatively drier-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight only<br/><small>No formal operating calendar or trail service exists.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Libreville</td><td>Car / local rider</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: the <a href="https://www.wikiloc.com/mountain-biking-trails/abaga-60566449">recorded Abaga MTB loop</a> and the <a href="https://mapcarta.com/es/17146370">Ikoï Mondah forest location reference</a>. Verify the current route and permissions locally.</i>]]></description>
