  <Placemark>
    <name>Maïdo Megavalanche Descent (Réunion) [shuttle]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Iconic mass-start descent from the Maïdo highlands</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Maïdo descent is Réunion's internationally known Mégavalanche venue and a major mass start race course. Its huge drop toward the west coast crosses exposed volcanic highland, tamarind forest and increasingly tropical lower slopes, with fast, rough and technical terrain for experienced riders.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No permanent lift, but commercial shuttle and guided services run from the west coast. Arrange an uplift and current route guidance rather than attempting an unsupported road return.<br/><br/><p class="warn">&#9888;&#65039; This is a long mountain descent, not a continuously maintained park line. Fog, rain, erosion, forestry closures and mixed-use sections can change it quickly; verify every segment and carry repair equipment.</p>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 May; closed from 1 December (cooler and generally drier-season indication).<br/>Daily opening hours: guided daylight access only<br/><small>No fixed operating calendar; shuttle schedules and forest closures determine access.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Saint-Gilles-les-Bains</td><td>Booked MTB shuttle</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: the <a href="https://www.reunion.fr/organisez/vos-activites/pour-un-souvenir-immanquable/vtt-velo-a-la-reunion-des-chemins-de-sable-aux-forets-de-tamarins/">official Réunion tourism MTB guide naming the Maïdo Mégavalanche and shuttle</a> and a <a href="https://reunionmountainbike.fr/">local Maïdo guided operator</a>. Check ONF closures before riding.</i>]]></description>
