  <Placemark>
    <name>Nesbyen MTB (Norway) [shuttle]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Norway's best-known shuttle-served gravity trail hub</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Nesbyen combines rough natural enduro descents around Trytetjern with purpose-built trails for several levels. HallingSpranget is the signature blue route: 17 km from Syningen on Nesfjellet to the town centre, losing about 1,000 vertical metres.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Trailhead Nesbyen runs fixed-route gravity shuttles between Blingsmovegen and Trytetjern. The separate FjellLinken bike bus serves the HallingSpranget start; advance booking is recommended.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Typically May-October, depending on snow and trail conditions. HallingSpranget is aiming for an early June opening in 2026, with bookings available from 13 June and daily summer shuttle service.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:30<br/><small>Typical gravity-shuttle window; HallingSpranget bus times and autumn operating days differ.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Nesbyen centre</td><td>Bike shuttle</td><td>~25-40 min to trailheads</td></tr><tr><td>Oslo</td><td>Train / car</td><td>~2h30-3h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.trailheadnesbyen.no/en/shuttling">Trailhead Nesbyen shuttle</a> and <a href="https://www.hallingspranget.no/en/">official HallingSpranget site</a>. Pin marks the OSM-mapped HallingSpranget start at Syningen, officially described as roughly 1,100 m.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>9.059966,60.532437,1046</coordinates></Point>
