  <Placemark>
    <name>Cerler Bike Park (Pyrenees, ES) [chairlift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Cerler - Spain's highest Pyrenean bike park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Part of the Aramon group, Cerler is one of Spain's most established lift-served bike parks in the Benasque valley. Trails range from green flow to technical black DH through the Pyrenean forest, with the Aneto massif as backdrop.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Chairlift carries bikes during summer operation. Check the current bike ticket and season dates with Aramon Cerler before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from June; closed from September (estimated summer season).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Huesca</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>Zaragoza</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.cerler.com/en/summer/bike-park">Cerler</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
