  <Placemark>
    <name>El Colorado Bike Park (Chile) [chairlift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>El Colorado - Santiago's closest lift-served park in the Andes</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The nearest chairlift-served bike park to Santiago, sharing the Farellones massif with Valle Nevado and La Parva. Trails descend through Andean scree and alpine terrain at 2500-3300 m with views of the capital below and Aconcagua on clear days.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Chairlift carries bikes during the December-March summer season. Bike passes may be shared with neighbouring Valle Nevado. Check the current tariff and lift schedule before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from December; closed from March (southern hemisphere summer).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Estimated hours; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Santiago</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://elcolorado.cl/">El Colorado</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
