  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Bikepark Spicak: valley station</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Spicak 1198 m - top of the Spicak chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The biggest bike park in Czechia and the one Czech and German riders treat as home. Around a dozen lines off a 330 m vertical: green flow, the long Traverz, several red jump lines and black rock and root tech, plus a dirt-jump area and a 4X track at the base. A second chairlift climbs on to Pancir 1214 m for the longer natural descents. Dense Sumava spruce forest, so it rides well in the heat and turns greasy fast in the wet.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Spicak chairlift from Zelezna Ruda carries bikes; a day ticket is 940 CZK for adults, 800 CZK for youth and 420 CZK for children, and tickets are issued on a chip card with a 50 CZK refundable deposit. Five-ride tickets (700 CZK) suit a short visit. The park is in the Gravity Card network.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 May; closed from 1 November (typical window; check the operator and conditions). Weekends only in May, then daily from 15 June.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Prague</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr><tr><td>Munich</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.spicak.cz/">Bikepark Spicak</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-gray</styleUrl>
