  <Placemark>
    <name>Chapelco: base station</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Cota 1600 - top of the Telecabina Chapelco</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Seven marked descents for every level, dropping through lenga forest on the flank of Cerro Chapelco above San Martin de los Andes. A new ten-seat gondola opened for 2026, linking the base to Cota 1600 in about five minutes and carrying up to 3000 people an hour, which transforms how many laps a day is worth. Southern-hemisphere season, so it runs while the Alps are shut.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Unlimited gondola laps with a bike pass; bring your own bike and helmet. The operator publishes winter skiing rates well ahead but had not posted a summer bike-park tariff at the time of writing, so no price is recorded here - check cerrochapelco.com.ar.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 15 December; closed from 16 April (typical southern-summer window; confirm dates with the operator).<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>San Martin de los Andes</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Bariloche</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.cerrochapelco.com.ar/">Cerro Chapelco</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
