  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Tamarancho - Fairfax, CA [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Camp Tamarancho trailhead at 230 m - permit-based natural singletrack in Marin County</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>An ~11-mile loop of hand-built, bike-legal singletrack on Boy Scouts of America property west of Fairfax. The clockwise loop climbs Alchemist Trail (uphill only as of 2026), then Goldman, Serpentine, Wagon Wheel and B-17 trails. Broken Dam Trail closes the loop. Endor Trail is a short, downhill-only flow trail with high berms and jumps; Caballo Rojo is another downhill-only option. Expect roots, rocks, switchbacks and the famous rock on Serpentine; Wagon Wheel adds rock gardens. Difficulty ranges from beginner-friendly sections to intermediate/advanced, with a few expert features.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Park in Fairfax and ride ~1.5 miles up Iron Springs Road to the trailhead kiosk. A permit is required and must be visible while riding. Day pass $6; annual single $50; family annual $75; Gold single $95; Gold family $135. Buy online from the Marin Council, BSA, or get day passes in person at Sunshine Bicycle Center in Fairfax. Class-1 eMTB only; no dogs; no riding when wet or muddy; no parking on Iron Springs Road.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; closed when trails are wet, raining or muddy after storms.<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Fairfax town center</td><td>Bike</td><td>~15 min climb</td></tr><tr><td>San Francisco</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h</td></tr><tr><td>Oakland</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.boyscouts-marin.org/tamarancho-mtn-biking/4023">Marin Council BSA - Tamarancho Mtn-Biking</a>, <a href="https://marintrailstewards.org/tamarancho">Marin Trail Stewards - Tamarancho Trail System</a>, <a href="https://tamarancho.report/passes/">Tamarancho Report - Passes</a>, <a href="https://www.mtbproject.com/trail/808937/camp-tamarancho-loop">MTB Project - Camp Tamarancho Loop</a> and <a href="https://bayarearides.com/rides/tamarancho/">Bay Area Rides - Camp Tamarancho</a>.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-122.612537,37.997046,233</coordinates></Point>
