  <Placemark>
    <name>China Camp State Park (California) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Pedal-accessed Bay Area trail system from sea level to ~320 m on San Pablo Bay</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>About 15 miles of multi-use trails wind through oak woodland, salt marsh and grassland. The Turtle Back Nature Trail is an easy, hiker-only ADA loop. For bikes, the Shoreline/Bayview Loop (6.9 mi, moderate) is the classic circuit, while Bay View/Bay Hills/Back Ranch Fire Trail (5.6 mi, strenuous) climbs San Pedro Mountain to ~320 m with views of Mount Tamalpais, Mount Diablo and the Coast Range. Terrain ranges from mellow fire road to rocky, rutted descents.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal up on park roads and fire roads. Vehicle day-use fee is $5 per car; annual California State Parks passes are accepted. Friends of China Camp annual pass/membership also available.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round, 8 a.m. to sunset daily. Coastal-temperate climate: winter ~10-15 C, summer ~20-30 C; mornings can be foggy.<br/><small>Class I pedal-assist e-bikes only, max 15 mph (5 mph on blind corners and when passing). Dogs are not allowed on trails.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>San Francisco</td><td>Car via Hwy 101 / N. San Pedro Rd</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>San Rafael</td><td>Car / bike</td><td>~15 min / direct</td></tr><tr><td>China Camp Village trailhead</td><td>Bike</td><td>Direct</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=466">California State Parks - China Camp State Park</a>, <a href="https://friendsofchinacamp.org/visit-the-park/activities/">Friends of China Camp - Activities and Trails</a>, <a href="https://friendsofchinacamp.org/e-bike-dos-and-donts-at-china-camp/">Friends of China Camp - E-bike rules</a>, OpenStreetMap/Nominatim and OpenTopoData for coordinates and elevation.</i>]]></description>
