  <Placemark>
    <name>Arkytox Bike Park (Aguascalientes) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Trailhead base 1,890 m</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A community-driven mountain bike park specialising in MTB Enduro riding. The network features a well-balanced mix of technical handling sections and fast, flowy tracks suitable for progressing riders. Built and maintained by the active local trail-building community, Arkytox offers fun, accessible terrain in a collaborative atmosphere.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal-up / self-shuttle access. Free entry, open 24 hours daily.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round.<br/>Daily opening hours: 24 hours<br/>
    <small>Peak times: Sunday mornings and weekend afternoons. Least crowded: Monday and Thursday evenings.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Aguascalientes</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Mexico City</td><td>Car</td><td>~5 h 30</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: local trail information and community riding reports. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-102.2472,21.8596,1939</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="spot"><value>arkytox</value></Data>
      <Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park no-lift enduro</value></Data>
      <Data name="open_from"><value>01-01</value></Data>
      <Data name="closed_from"><value>01-01</value></Data>
    </ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Yuca Xtreme Bike Park (Aguascalientes) [100 MXN]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Bottom shuttle base 2,580 m</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>High-altitude forested bike park in the Sierra Fría, featuring 12 designated trails primarily designed for All-Mountain and Downhill disciplines. Standout lines include Bosquecito, a highly rated flowy blue track with rock gardens, and Camino Ancho Yuca Xtreme, a challenging green line featuring a steep black-diamond style climb. The park is fully shuttle-accessible for easy uplifts through pine forest terrain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Vehicular shuttle trucks. Day ticket approximately 100 MXN; confirm current pricing. Private property park requiring day-pass purchase.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 April; closed from 1 November (typical season for high-altitude forest riding).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-18:00<br/>
    <small>Estimated hours; check with the operator for current shuttle schedules and reservation requirements.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Aguascalientes</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 15</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Mexico City</td><td>Car</td><td>~6 h</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: regional trail network documentation and shuttle operator information. Prices, schedules and shuttle availability can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-102.3920,21.8491,1925</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData>
      <Data name="spot"><value>yuca-xtreme</value></Data>
      <Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh</value></Data>
