  <Placemark>
    <name>Parque Barrancas Trail Network (San Rafael) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Top trailhead hub 2,120 m - canyon edge</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Grand canyon enduro network in the dramatic San Rafael area of Chihuahua, frequently associated with the sweeping Copper Canyon region landscape. Built primarily as an Enduro and rugged All-Mountain network featuring raw, highly technical singletracks plunging down dramatic canyon topography. Standout lines include Ruta Panorámica, a scenic 7-mile blue singletrack lined with berms and ladder bridges, and Ruta Extrema El Lomo, a gnarly double-black diamond raw ridge descent dropping 1,901 vertical feet.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal-up or rugged point-to-point vehicle drops. Free access to natural trail network.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 April; closed from 1 November (estimated typical season for high-altitude canyon riding).<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/>
    <small>Remote terrain; carry navigation equipment and verify current trail conditions locally.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Chihuahua</td><td>Car</td><td>~4 h</td></tr>
      <tr><td>San Rafael village</td><td>Bike / 4x4</td><td>Direct</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: regional trail network documentation and rider reports. Trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-107.8307,27.5195,2254</coordinates></Point>
