  <Placemark>
    <name>La Fragua Bike Park (Guanajuato) [50 MXN]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Bottom shuttle base 2,230 m</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Private mountain property bike park high in the Sierra de Santa Rosa outside Guanajuato City. Features 13 technical trails tailored for All-Mountain, Enduro and Downhill disciplines. Boasts a massive 8,335 feet of total accumulated descent starting from a high peak elevation of 9,357 feet. Standout lines include Carbon Flow, a fast, heavily sculpted line featuring gap jumps, berms and wooden bridges, plus Cañada, a steep rock-strewn black diamond downhill-only singletrack. Highly rated on-site restaurant serving local food.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Vehicular shuttle trucks; e-bikes allowed. Requires private day-ticket pass approximately 50 MXN; confirm current pricing.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from 1 April; closed from 1 November (typical season for high-sierra riding).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-18:00<br/>
    <small>Estimated hours; confirm current shuttle schedules and day-pass requirements with the operator.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access">
      <tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Guanajuato City</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Mexico City</td><td>Car</td><td>~4 h</td></tr>
    </table><br/>
    <i>Sources: park operator information and regional trail network documentation. Prices, schedules, trail status and shuttle availability can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-101.2185,21.0827,2651</coordinates></Point>
