  <Placemark>
    <name>Keppoch Mountain (Nova Scotia, Canada) [shuttle]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Weekend shuttle drop-off around 218 m above Antigonish</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Almost 30 km of purpose-built mountain-bike trails range from beginner flow to expert natural and technical descents. The community-operated park also has a skills area, bike wash and repair station, and hosts downhill and enduro events.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Weekend bike shuttles carry riders to the upper trail network; pedal access is also possible. Buy a day or season pass through Keppoch and check capacity before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Published 2026 shuttle opening: 23 May. Standard service runs Saturday-Sunday, 10:00-17:00, generally through late October.<br/><small>Potential Friday evening services are announced separately.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Antigonish</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Halifax</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.thekeppoch.ca/events/bike-shuttle-opening-weekend">official 2026 shuttle opening</a> and <a href="https://novascotia.com/listing/keppoch-mountain/">Tourism Nova Scotia park information</a>. Pin marks the upper Summit West trailhead, elevation-checked at 218 m.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-62.113390,45.538780,218</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>ca-ns-keppoch</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert natural no-lift dh enduro freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>05-23</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>10-26</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Sugarloaf Bike Park (New Brunswick, Canada) [chairlift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sugarloaf 45 m - valley station of the chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>About 49 km of riding and 36 listed trails combine Gravity Logic-built flow, jump lines, drops and wooden features with rocky expert downhill and year-round cross-country trails. The lower mountain includes a family skills park and pump track.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The chairlift serves the downhill network. Published 2026 full-day tickets are CAD 47.52 adult and CAD 39.60 youth/student/senior; rentals and one-ride tickets are available.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Published 2026 bike-park season: 30 May-27 September. Weekends in spring and fall; Thursday-Sunday from late June through early September.<br/>Typical hours: 10:00-19:30 Thursday-Saturday and 10:00-16:30 Sunday in high summer.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Campbellton</td><td>Car / bike</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Bathurst</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://sugarloafbikepark.ca/bike-park/">official bike-park overview and trail totals</a>, <a href="https://sugarloafbikepark.ca/tickets-passes/">2026 tickets and schedule</a> and the OSM-mapped chairlift (ODbL). Pin marks its upper endpoint, verified at 195 m.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-66.695306,47.981508,47</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>ca-nb-sugarloaf</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>05-30</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>09-28</value></Data><mwm:icon>Transport</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Sugarloaf Bike Park: top of the chairlift</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Chairlift top station 195 m - Atlantic Canada's original lift-access bike park</b><br/><br/>
    Top station of the chairlift, where the descents start. See the main Sugarloaf Bike Park pin for trails, prices and access.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-gray</styleUrl>
