  <Placemark>
    <name>Poley Mountain Bike Park (New Brunswick, Canada) [chairlift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Poley Mountain 90 m - valley station of the Quad Chair</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A compact gravity park with beginner-friendly flow, natural intermediate and expert descents, jumps and technical forest sections. Riders can combine the lift-served network with pedal-access multi-use trails; bike rentals are available.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Quad Chair carries bikes. Poley sells day access and 2026 summer passes with or without chairlift access; the published adult lift-included season pass is CAD 300.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Published 2026 summer bike season runs June-October, with regular Friday-Sunday operations.<br/><small>Daily hours, lift choice and trail status vary; consult the current report before travelling.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Sussex</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Saint John / Moncton</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.poleymountain.com/">official 2026 summer bike information</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/257027285">OSM Quad Chair way 257027285</a> (ODbL). Pin marks the upper lift endpoint, verified at 278 m.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-65.381210,45.681907,89</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>ca-nb-poley</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>11-01</value></Data><mwm:icon>Transport</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Poley Mountain Bike Park: top of the Quad Chair</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Quad Chair top station 278 m - lift-served riding in the Waterford hills</b><br/><br/>
    Top station of the Quad Chair, where the descents start. See the main Poley Mountain Bike Park pin for trails, prices and access.]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-gray</styleUrl>
    <Point><coordinates>-65.376522,45.675925,278</coordinates></Point>
    <ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>ca-nb-poley</value></Data><mwm:icon>None</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark><name>Family Bike Park Zieleniec (PL) [cable car]</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Gryglowka and Nartorama - nearly 10 km of lift-served trails</b><br/><br/>Five signed routes range from gentle beginner flow to the steep natural Crazy Dad line. Cable cars carry bikes to the route starts; rentals and instruction are available.<br/><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://zieleniec.pl/en/lato/family-bike-park-zieleniec">official Family Bike Park Zieleniec</a>.</i>]]></description><styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>16.395700,50.336900,856</coordinates></Point><ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>zieleniec</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>05-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>10-31</value></Data><mwm:icon>Transport</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData></Placemark>
  <Placemark><name>Wierchomla Bike Park (PL) [chairlift]</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Dwie Doliny Wierchomla Mala - lift-served downhill and enduro</b><br/><br/>A Beskid gravity park with marked downhill and freeride lines, plus pedal-access forest routes. Expect natural roots and rocks between shaped sections.<br/><br/><i>Sources: <a href="https://www.polska.travel/park-rowerowy-wierchomla/">Poland Travel park profile</a> and <a href="https://www.wierchomla.com.pl/">Wierchomla resort</a>.</i>]]></description><styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>20.755500,49.365800,443</coordinates></Point><ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>wierchomla</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>expert bike-park dh enduro freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>09-30</value></Data><mwm:icon>Transport</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData></Placemark>
  <Placemark><name>Bike Park Kluszkowce (PL) [chairlift]</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Wdjar mountain above Kluszkowce - compact gravity riding</b><br/><br/>A purpose-built park on the Wdjar ski slope with downhill, flow and jump lines including the A-line. The chairlift serves bike routes during summer operations.<br/><br/><i>Source: <a href="https://czorsztyn.pl/">Czorsztyn municipality and resort information</a>; confirm current schedules locally.</i>]]></description><styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>20.300900,49.443500,524</coordinates></Point><ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>kluszkowce</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert bike-park dh enduro freeride</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>06-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>09-30</value></Data><mwm:icon>Transport</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData></Placemark>
  <Placemark><name>Wadi Degla Protectorate MTB (Egypt) [no lift]</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Desert valley trail network on Cairo's southeastern edge</b><br/><br/>Wadi Degla is a protected 30 km limestone valley with rocky and sandy tracks used by Cairo mountain bikers. This is natural cross-country and all-mountain riding, not a formal lift park.<br/><br/><i>Sources: <a href="https://cairo.gov.eg/ar/">Cairo Governorate reserve information</a> and local MTB route documentation.</i>]]></description><styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>31.340500,29.961500,129</coordinates></Point><ExtendedData xmlns:mwm="https://omaps.app"><Data name="spot"><value>egypt-wadi-degla</value></Data><Data name="tags"><value>beginner expert natural no-lift enduro</value></Data><Data name="open_from"><value>01-01</value></Data><Data name="closed_from"><value>01-01</value></Data><mwm:icon>Mountain</mwm:icon><mwm:visibility>1</mwm:visibility></ExtendedData></Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Weissenstein: Flowtrail</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>1.8 km marked flow trail</b><br/><br/>Built MTB flow trail descending from the Weissenstein gondola area toward Oberdorf, with berms, rollers and intermediate features.<br/><br/><i>Geometry simplified from <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/1148325073">OpenStreetMap way 1148325073</a> (ODbL). Trail description and lift context: <a href="https://www.seilbahn-weissenstein.ch/">Seilbahn Weissenstein</a>. Indicative line; follow local signs and conditions.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#line-trail</styleUrl>
    <LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>7.508076,47.245373,0 7.506748,47.244962,0 7.505005,47.245061,0 7.504968,47.244842,0 7.503862,47.244872,0 7.503459,47.244727,0 7.503149,47.244798,0 7.503279,47.244703,0 7.502620,47.244674,0 7.502698,47.244559,0 7.501732,47.244621,0 7.501638,47.244555,0 7.501921,47.244448,0 7.501573,47.244380,0 7.501439,47.244139,0 7.501178,47.244175,0 7.500921,47.244009,0 7.500513,47.243948,0 7.499937,47.244066,0 7.500060,47.243832,0 7.498596,47.243884,0 7.499028,47.243627,0 7.497758,47.243693,0 7.496745,47.243635,0 7.496472,47.243515,0 7.496280,47.243669,0 7.495735,47.243325,0 7.494828,47.243351,0 7.494764,47.243245,0 7.494115,47.243197,0 7.492794,47.242824,0 7.492443,47.243039,0 7.492500,47.242579,0 7.492199,47.242244,0 7.491279,47.241744,0</coordinates></LineString>
