  <Placemark>
    <name>Bareges - Grand Tourmalet Bike Park (Hautes-Pyrenees) [24 EUR, closed 2026]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Tournaboup 1460 m - valley station of the Tournaboup chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/><b>Closed for the summer 2026 season</b> while the Grand Tourmalet lift system is rebuilt; a faster lift is planned for summer 2027. When it runs, the park has 12 routes off the Tournaboup chairlift and shuttle: a beginner area with 1 green downhill and 3 green enduro routes, then 2 blue, 1 red and 2 black downhill runs. Marked enduro valley routes continue down towards Luz-Saint-Sauveur from the same base.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Tournaboup chairlift, plus a free shuttle running twice a day, seven days a week, from the surrounding villages. Day pass 24 EUR when operating.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Not operating in summer 2026 - major lift works on the Grand Tourmalet domain. Expected to return with a new lift in summer 2027.<br/><small>Confirm with the operator before planning a trip.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lourdes</td><td>Shuttle</td><td>~1h00</td></tr><tr><td>Tarbes</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.n-py.com/fr/grand-tourmalet/bike-park">Grand Tourmalet bike park</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
