  <Placemark>
    <name>Bikepark Lienz - Hochstein (East Tyrol) [40 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lienz 680 m - valley station of the Schlossbergbahn</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Four to five singletracks over about 12 km on the Hochstein: one blue, two red and one black, marketed as Flow, Medium, Enduro and the Pro or Sagan line. The vertical is the point - 1310 m from the top of the Hochstein t-bar down to the town, which is a lot for a park you can ride to from a railway station. Using the trails is free; you only pay to be carried up.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Schlossbergbahn from Lienz at 680 m, then the Hochstein two-seat chairlift and the t-bar above it. Day ticket around 40 EUR adult, 26 EUR child; some 2026 listings quote up to 48 EUR, so check before you buy.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from mid-May; closed from the end of October, daily through the main season.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Published operating hours; check the lift calendar.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lienz station</td><td>Bike</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Innsbruck</td><td>Train</td><td>~3h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.lienzer-bergbahnen.at/en/summer-activities/biking/bike-park-lienz/">Lienzer Bergbahnen</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
