  <Placemark>
    <name>San Martino Bike Arena - Tognola (Dolomites) [27 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>San Martino di Castrozza 1405 m - valley station of the Tognola gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Four downhill tracks off the Tognola, three of them over 2 km: Tognola DH1, 3.4 km and 500 m of drop from 2200 m, red; Tognola DH2, 2.1 km and 300 m, red; and the blue Variante DH3, 2.9 km, for riders not ready for the reds. The Colverde gondola opens the panoramic side at 2000 m. The Pale di San Martino stand over the whole thing, which is most of the reason to come.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Tognola cable car climbs over 700 m to 2200 m in ten minutes; the Colverde gondola serves the other sector. Bike pass 27 EUR a day, 48 EUR for two consecutive days, 200 EUR for the season.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from late June; closed from mid-September (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 08:30-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Feltre</td><td>Bus</td><td>~1h20</td></tr><tr><td>Trento</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://sanmartinobikearena.com/">San Martino Bike Arena</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
