  <Placemark>
    <name>Schoeckl Trail Area (Graz, Styria) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>St Radegund 780 m - valley station of the Schoecklseilbahn</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Eleven tracks on 655 m of vertical, in four main lines covering downhill, freeride, single trail and a table line. Gedscho is the one people talk about: a European championship course almost twenty years ago and still among the hardest trails anywhere. Gibim, Hintnumi and Silent Hill are not far behind it. The newer 1000er is an enduro line that runs all the way off the mountain into Stattegg on the edge of Graz, so you can finish a lap in the city.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Schoeckl cable car climbs the 655 m in seven minutes and runs all year, Monday to Sunday, closing only for maintenance in spring and for two or three weeks in November. Prices are set by Holding Graz - check before travel.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Runs year-round apart from maintenance closures in spring and November.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:30<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Graz</td><td>Bus</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Vienna</td><td>Train + bus</td><td>~3h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.schoeckl-trail-area.at/trail-area/trails/">Schoeckl Trail Area</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
