  <Placemark>
    <name>Bikepark Braunlage - Wurmberg (Harz, Germany) [38 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Braunlage 575 m - valley station of the Wurmbergseilbahn</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Four trails on northern Germany's highest lift-served hill, up to 4 km long and all on natural ground rather than shaped dirt: Freeride, Snakebite, Evil Rock's and Enduro. Using the trails costs nothing - you buy a gondola ticket and that is it, which is an unusually honest arrangement.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Wurmberg six-seat gondola from Braunlage at 575 m to 971 m; the Hexen-Express chairlift serves the upper part. Day ticket 38 EUR adult, 27 EUR for under-18s and students; five-trip card 20 EUR, ten-trip 40 EUR.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from May; closed from November (typical window; check the operator and conditions).<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><small>Typical daily estimate; check the operator schedule.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Goslar</td><td>Bus</td><td>~1h00</td></tr><tr><td>Hanover</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://wurmberg-seilbahn.de/bikepark.html">Wurmbergseilbahn</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
