  <Placemark>
    <name>Pic du Jer Bike Park - Lourdes (Hautes-Pyrenees) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lourdes 415 m - valley station of the Pic du Jer funicular</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Small in count and serious in pedigree: a blue downhill that rides as a flow trail, a black downhill built for experts and racers, and a red enduro line for confident riders, all dropping about 600 m off the Pic du Jer straight above Lourdes. Single track, berms, technical sections and rolling ground in the same run. The hill has held four UCI World Cups and its 2015 round was voted the best of the series.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The historic Pic du Jer funicular, departing every 20 minutes from 10:00 to 17:00 and to 18:00 in summer, carrying a maximum of 12 bikes per cabin. Half-day and day passes; check the operator for current rates.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open from spring to autumn; check the operator for the exact window.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-17:00, to 18:00 in summer<br/><small>Departures every 20 minutes; 12 bikes per cabin, so expect a queue on a busy day.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Lourdes station</td><td>Bike</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Toulouse</td><td>Train</td><td>~1h50</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.picdujer.com/descendre-en-vtt">Pic du Jer</a>.
    Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
