  <Placemark>
    <name>Trail Area Turracher Hoehe (Carinthia/Styria) [45 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Turrach 1390 m - valley station of the Turrachbahn</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Twelve signed trails in the Nockberge, built around the 5.6 km Kornock Flowtrail - an intermediate S1 line with a few S2 sections that runs from the top down past the turquoise Turracher See. Around it: the Zirben Trail (700 m) and Schmuggler Trail (690 m), both S2, the short and steep Earl Grey (100 m), the Tea House Trail (1.2 km, hard to very hard), the UeWI Jump Trail (485 m of S3-S4 jumps), the easier UeWI Flowtrail (500 m), Stone Pine Trail (700 m), Almrush and Ibahaps (200 m each), the Kornock Drop and a connecting trail. A kids and practice area at the valley station adds a mini skill trail, Nocky's Kids Loop and a small pump track.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Kornockbahn cable car takes riders and bikes up. Day pass 45 EUR adult, 27 EUR child (6-14); single ascent with a bike 25 EUR adult, 15 EUR child.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>20 June to 30 September. Daily until mid-September, then weekends only.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-16:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Villach</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr><tr><td>Salzburg</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.turracherhoehe.at/en/summer/mountain-biking/trails">Turracher Hoehe cable cars</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> (ODbL) for the trail geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
