  <Placemark>
    <name>Nara Bike Park - Leontica (Ticino) [39 CHF]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Leontica 925 m - valley station of the Leontica-Cancori chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The Black Wood Line is the reason to come: Ticino's first flow trail built for mountain bikes only and served by a lift, with difficulty varying along its length so a family and a fast rider can both use it. Three natural enduro descents complete the area - Cancori Bike, Brusacu Bike and Negrentino Bike - dropping from Cancori through chestnut woods to Leontica, two of them part of the SwitzerlandMobility network.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Two chairlift sections from Leontica at 925 m: Leontica-Cancori, then Cancori-Pian Nara. Bike day pass 39 CHF adult or 99 CHF for a family; single ascent 19 CHF adult, 59 CHF family; season pass 259 CHF, which includes half price on the Airolo MTB day ticket.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>7 June to 11 October. Saturdays, Sundays and holidays, plus daily from 1 to 16 August. First section 09:00-12:30 and 16:00-17:30, second section 09:00-16:00.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Biasca</td><td>Bus</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Bellinzona</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://narabikepark.ch/">Nara Bike Park</a>, <a href="https://nara.ch/tariffe-estate/">Nara summer tariffs</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> (ODbL) for the trail geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
