  <Placemark>
    <name>Bike Park de Cormaranche-en-Bugey (Ain) [free]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Cormaranche-en-Bugey 940 m - village access to the Terre Ronde trails; the descents drop from the plateau at about 1234 m</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Thirteen trails in the southern Jura, an hour and a quarter from both Lyon and Geneva: seven downhill runs, five marked enduro loops and a Ludik Park for children from eight. Downhill, longest first: Chicken Lane and Bugey Libre (1.7 km each, the second a freeride line), Junior (1.9 km, intermediate), Tagada (1.8 km, beginner), Cormavalanche (1.65 km, expert), Johnny (600 m of flow) and Voltage (400 m, steep and technical). The enduro routes run E1 Le Reservoir (3.75 km, easiest) through E3 Golet Marmier (6.6 km, hard) and E4 Mazieres (7.4 km, very hard) to E5 La Pierre a l'Ours, 8.2 km and long but manageable.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No summer lift. Riding the park is free and open all year; the uplift is a paid shuttle at 18 EUR a day, 14 EUR a half day or 3 EUR a single run. It runs weekends and holidays from late April to early June, Thursday to Sunday in July and August, weekends from mid-September to early November, and over the Christmas holidays when the weather allows. Otherwise pedal or arrange your own car.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Trails open year round, daily, except when there is snow on the plateau. Shuttle days as above.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Ambronay</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Lyon</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
<i>Sources: <a href="https://bikeparkcormaranche.wixsite.com/accueil">Bike Park Cormaranche</a> and <a href="https://www.hautbugey-tourisme.com/equipement/bike-park-pistes-vtt-enduro-et-descente/">Haut-Bugey Tourisme</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
