  <Placemark>
    <name>Bikepark Albstadt (Swabian Alb, Germany) [24 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Albstadt-Tailfingen 825 m - valley station of the Schalkental drag lift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Eight lines in the Schalkental valley below Tailfingen, graded across the full range from 1 to 5: Flowline, Nordschleife, Loam Line, Mini Downhill, Rookie Run, Castle Trail, Eight Ball and a Jump Line, with plenty of jump variants and individual lines within each track. The loam holds up well in the wet, which is why the park has a following in shoulder season. A workshop on site handles mechanicals.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A drag lift run by WSV Tailfingen pulls riders up to the start tower of the downhill track. Day ticket 24 EUR adult, 20 EUR youth; five rides 13 EUR, ten rides 24 EUR; eleven days 240 EUR and 200 EUR; season pass 349 EUR for 2026, which pays off from about the twelfth visit. Cash, debit and credit cards accepted.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer season; the operator publishes its lift days in a seasonal flyer rather than a fixed calendar, so check before setting off.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Albstadt-Ebingen</td><td>Bike</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Stuttgart</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://bikepark-albstadt.de/">Bikepark Albstadt</a> and <a href="https://www.albstadt-tourismus.de/attraktion/bikepark-albstadt-105bb9451a">Albstadt Tourismus</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
