  <Placemark>
    <name>Tamarack Bike Park (Idaho) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Tamarack 1490 m - valley station of the Tamarack Express</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>About 520 m (1700 ft) of gravity-fed descent on a 3500-acre independent resort 90 miles north of Boise, running from flat green runs through a big intermediate middle to double-black lines - flowing singletrack and clean berms at one end, rock gardens and tabletops at the other. Trails mapped on the mountain include Super G and Show-Low, Pura Vida and Waltz on the easier side, Merlin and Wild Turkey through the middle, and Hot Shot and Smokejumper at the hard end.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Tamarack Express chairlift. Day tickets and season passes are sold through the resort's booking portal, which rewards buying at least ten days ahead; the resort does not print a window rate. Tamarack Outfitters, +1 208 325 1030, will quote it.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The Tamarack Express and the downhill bike park run through the summer season.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>McCall</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Boise</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://tamarackidaho.com/tickets-passes">Tamarack Resort tickets and passes</a>, <a href="https://visitidaho.org/travel-tips/experience-mountain-rush-tamaracks-bike-park/">Visit Idaho</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> (ODbL) for the trail names and geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
