  <Placemark>
    <name>Windham Mountain Bike Park (New York) [members and lodging guests]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Windham 520 m - valley station of the Westside Six</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Windham's downhill terrain has real pedigree - the mountain ran UCI World Cup downhill rounds for years - but the operation has changed shape. Since the resort became Windham Mountain Club, on-mountain biking is an amenity for members and lodging guests rather than a ticketed public bike park, delivered as guided rides for all abilities with a premium e-bike rental fleet.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Westside Six chairlift serves the mountain. There is no public day ticket: access comes with membership, or with a Mountainside or Outpost lodging package. Book through the club, +1 800 754 9463.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer and autumn, on club hours: 09:00-16:00 on weekdays, 08:00-16:00 at weekends.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Albany</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr><tr><td>New York City</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.windhammountainclub.com/mountain-biking/">Windham Mountain Club</a> and <a href="https://www.windhammountainclub.com/lift-tickets/">Windham Mountain Club tickets</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
