  <Placemark>
    <name>Les Carroz Bike Park - Grand Massif (Haute-Savoie) [20 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Les Carroz 1160 m - valley station of the Kedeuze gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Seven runs and more than 14 km of descent between 1140 m and 1760 m, spanning a family blue at one end and a double black that has held French championship rounds at the other. Woody Woodbiker is the one most people come for: over 5 km of blue from the top of the gondola back to the village, past Gron lake with a picnic area on the way. The park is shaped by hand rather than by machine, and the Bike Patrol goes over it daily.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The eight-seat Kedeuze gondola. One MTB ascent with bike-park access 11 EUR, a day pass 20 EUR, and twelve ascents 55 EUR. Passes are sold at the gondola ticket office and from 24-hour machines.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>20 June to 6 September 2026, daily.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Cluses</td><td>Bus</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Geneva</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.lescarroz.com/en/activities/bike-park/">Les Carroz bike park</a> and <a href="https://reservation.lescarroz.com/forfaits-bike-park.html">Les Carroz bike-park passes</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
