  <Placemark>
    <name>FolgaRide Bike Park - Alpe Cimbra (Trentino) [30 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Francolini 1175 m - valley station of the Sommo Alto gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Two long flow tracks off Sommo Alto, both dropping 325 m: FolgaLine, 4.4 km of light blue built from banked corners, linked turns and small rollers, and FolgaBolic, 3.8 km of red with parabolic berms, rollers and jumps. A third line, Folga Natural, is announced. The Skill Area at Serrada adds a pump track and a Baby Bike Park for three- to six-year-olds, and the FolgaRide trail centre at the base has rental, a workshop and an MTB school. The Alpe Cimbra route network and the separate Lavarone bike park - Rum Runner, Mojito, Pina Colada and Whezzy - are part of the same ticket area.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Francolini-Sommo Alto gondola and the Serrada-Dosso Martinella chairlift. Bike Pass 30 EUR adult a day down to 15 EUR child, seven days 108 EUR adult; children born 2018 or later ride free with a paying adult. Carrying a bike on the Folgaria and Lavarone chairlifts on its own is 3 EUR. Residents get 20 percent off and Guest Card holders 10.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>30 May to 2 June 2026, then weekends in mid-June, then daily from 19 June to 13 September.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:30-17:30<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Rovereto</td><td>Bus</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Trento</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.alpecimbrabike.it/en/bike-park/bike-park-folgaria/">Alpe Cimbra Bike - Folgaria</a> and <a href="https://www.alpecimbra.it/it/homepage/bike-park-e-pump-track/1350-25909.html">Alpe Cimbra tourism board</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
