  <Placemark>
    <name>Piana di Vigezzo Bike Land (Piedmont) [25 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Prestinone 805 m - valley station of the Piana di Vigezzo gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Vigezzo Bike Land is a set of downhill and enduro routes reached by the Prestinone gondola, and from the top you pick one of three directions - Craveggia, Arvogno or Montenero. Only Craveggia is fair game with minimal experience; the other two have technical sections and want real downhill technique. The named lines are the Woodpecker flow trail, easy and over 6 km; Smooth Roots, a 5.8 km intermediate enduro descent built in 2022 for about 600 m of drop; and the Downhill track, very fast and very technical, which held regional championship rounds in 2008.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Prestinone-Piana di Vigezzo gondola. A day pass is 25 EUR with a downhill bike, 15 EUR with an ordinary mountain bike. Guided riding is 85 EUR a half day and 150 EUR a full day, and rental is available at the gondola station, in Santa Maria Maggiore and at Druogno.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer gondola season.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Domodossola</td><td>Centovalli train</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Locarno</td><td>Centovalli train</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://pianadivigezzo.it/en/pages/bike-area">Piana di Vigezzo bike area</a>, <a href="http://www.vallevigezzo.eu/bike-e-downhill/">Valle Vigezzo tourism</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> (ODbL) for the trail geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
