  <Placemark>
    <name>Camp Fortune Bike Park (Quebec) [45 CAD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Chelsea 175 m - valley station of the Meech chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Over 20 km of trail in the Gatineau Hills, fifteen minutes from downtown Ottawa, shared with walkers and runners. The operator is honest that it suits advanced beginners upward and is really an intermediate-to-expert hill. Mapped descents include Coupe Quebec and National - race lines - plus Oz, Sentier Horizon at the very hard end, Switchback, Glap, Sunset and the gentler Junior.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A chairlift serves the downhill trails. A lift-served day is 40 CAD on Wednesday and Thursday evenings and 45 CAD at weekends, with a 375 CAD season pass; everything is bought online onto a reusable RFID card, which costs 5 CAD once and is not refundable.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Late June to Thanksgiving Monday, on Wednesdays, Thursdays and weekends.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Ottawa</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Montreal</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://campfortune.com/en/mountain-biking/">Camp Fortune mountain biking</a>, <a href="https://campfortune.com/en/lift-tickets/">Camp Fortune lift tickets</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> (ODbL) for the trail names and geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-blue</styleUrl>
