  <Placemark>
    <name>Ramundbergets Cykelpark (Harjedalen, Sweden) [190 SEK]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Ramundberget 750 m - valley station of the Fjallgardsbanan</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Machine-built flow trails through mountain birch and past waterfalls, graded green for smooth flow, blue for sharper corners and red for the steepest ground, biggest drops and technical sections, with orange marking paths shared with walkers. A technique area at the top steps up through drops and rock features. Green and blue do not need a full-suspension bike, which is the point - this is a park a family can ride together, with rest areas, grill spots and a zip line along the Helagsflytet trail.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The lift from the village up to the summit near Restaurant Tusen. The Fjallpass Cykel is the ticket worth knowing about: one pass covers all of Funasfjallen - 180 km of mountain trail, 31 bike-park trails and three summer lift systems at Ramundberget, Tanndalen and Funasdalsberget - with a reusable access card at 65 SEK on top.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer; the resort gives dates by phone (+46 684 66 88 00) rather than on a fixed calendar.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Funasdalen</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Ostersund</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.ramundberget.se/se-och-gora/sommaraktiviteter/fjallcykling/cykelpark/">Ramundberget cykelpark</a> and <a href="https://www.ramundberget.se/information/liftkort/sommar/">Ramundberget summer lift passes</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
