  <Placemark>
    <name>Falls Creek Bike Park (Victoria, Australia) [commercial shuttle]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Falls Creek 1515 m - valley station of the Gully chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Fifty kilometres of gravity trail across 21 runs, designed and built by World Trail, with over 10 km of it aimed at beginners - unusually generous for an Australian alpine park. Flowtown is the long one at 5.1 km, and the rest of the network reads Skyline, The Generator, Jumpstart, Thunderbolt, High Voltage, Frying Pan Spur, The Vortex, Blackout, Wishing Well, Lakeview and Turbine. Snow-gum alpine terrain rather than forest loam. Trails close on event weekends.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No summer chairlift.</b> Uplift is a commercial shuttle run by Blue Dirt Mountain Biking, operating Thursday to Monday from the village hub with additional pick-up points; buy a ticket online the day before or on the day at the Village Bike Cafe. The resort does not publish the shuttle fare on its own page.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The Australian summer - roughly November to April, opposite the ski season.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Mount Beauty</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Melbourne</td><td>Car</td><td>~4h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.fallscreek.com.au/summer/summer-activities/mountain-biking/">Falls Creek mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> (ODbL) for the trail names and geometry. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
