  <Placemark>
    <name>Glencoe Mountain Bike Park (Scotland) [35 GBP]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Glencoe 365 m - valley station of the access chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Two downhill tracks with a real reputation on the West Highland hillside: a fast, flowing Red that was substantially rebuilt and now runs five sections of back-to-back berms, bumps and jumps with a flow section added in 2023, and a rough, rowdy Black - steep, very rocky, hairpins, berms and drops, and genuinely only for riders with downhill experience. Newer Blue, Red and Black cross-country trails also start from the top of the chairlift, and the valley floor has the West Highland Way, the Old Military Road and the Rannoch path for anyone wanting distance instead.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The chairlift, with bikes hooked to a chair by the seatpost. An uplift day is 35 GBP adult, 25 GBP junior; a single chairlift ride 20 GBP adult, 15 GBP junior. Bike hire on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Mid-May to late October, weather permitting. Chairlift from 09:00, last uplift 16:15.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-16:15<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Fort William</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Glasgow</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.glencoemountain.co.uk/mountain-biking/">Glencoe Mountain Resort biking</a> and <a href="https://www.glencoemountain.co.uk/prices/">Glencoe Mountain Resort summer prices</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
