  <Placemark>
    <name>Sir Sam's Bike Park (Haliburton, Ontario) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Haliburton 360 m - valley station of the 4x4 chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Over 23 km of cross-country and downhill trail across open meadow, hardwood forest and old rock outcrops in the Haliburton Highlands - 17 of the hill's 27 trails are open to bikes. Modest vertical, but the rock makes up for it.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A surface lift you walk on and off carries riders to the top today; a new Doppelmayr quad is being installed from spring 2026 and opens for the 2026-27 season. The resort does not publish a summer bike rate online.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Spring to mid-October, open daily.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Haliburton</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Toronto</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.sirsams.ca/">Sir Sam's Ski / Ride</a> and <a href="https://thehighlander.ca/2026/01/08/sir-sams-new-lift-for-2027/">The Highlander on the new lift</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
