  <Placemark>
    <name>Parc du Mont-Comi Bike Park (Quebec) [25 CAD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Saint-Donat 285 m - valley station of the Mont-Comi lifts</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Twenty-four trails over 25 km on 306 m of vertical in the Bas-Saint-Laurent, and the grading tells you what it is: 6 green, 7 blue, 8 black and 3 double black. The descent sector is among the hardest and most technical in Quebec. The station has since cut two easier descents from the summit so beginners and intermediates can ride down from the top as well. Helmets are compulsory across the whole network.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Chairlift 2 runs for riders and walkers on Sundays, 11:00-16:00. A day is 25 CAD, taxes included.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer, then the Belles Fins de Semaine d'Automne from mid-September to mid-October, Saturdays and Sundays.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Rimouski</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Quebec City</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://mont-comi.ca/en/mountain-biking/">Parc du Mont-Comi mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://sentiersdumontcomi.com/">Les Sentiers du Mont-Comi</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
