  <Placemark>
    <name>Magic Mountain (Vermont) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Londonderry 420 m - valley station of the Red Chair</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Magic is a cult southern-Vermont ski hill - fifty runs, some of the steepest lift-served terrain in New England, two chairlifts and two surface lifts - but it is a winter operation first and does not publish a summer bike-park product. Treat it as ski-area terrain rather than a graded park, and check with the mountain before planning a day's riding around it.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No published summer lift-served biking.</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer and autumn, subject to what the mountain chooses to run.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Manchester VT</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Boston</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.magicmtn.com/">Magic Mountain Ski Area</a> and <a href="https://www.magicmtn.com/lift-ticket-info">Magic Mountain ticket info</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
