  <Placemark>
    <name>49 Degrees North (Chewelah, Washington) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Chewelah 1200 m - valley station of the Northern Spirit Express</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A big ski area in the Colville National Forest on Chewelah Peak, 50 miles north of Spokane: 2300 acres, seven lifts and 90 marked winter runs over 1871 ft of vertical. For summer, though, the resort publishes no bike-park trail list or bike tariff - its warm-season programme centres on the nordic centre and fat-bike access. Ride the forest here on its own terms, and confirm before counting on a lift.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No published summer bike operation.</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer, once the forest roads and trails dry out.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Chewelah</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Spokane</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.ski49n.com/">49 Degrees North Mountain Resort</a> and <a href="https://shop.ski49n.com/seasonpasses">49 Degrees North passes</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
