  <Placemark>
    <name>Red River (New Mexico) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Red River 2635 m - valley station of the Platinum chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Red River Ski and Summer Area sits above a small town at the top of the Enchanted Circle, with 64 winter runs and 1600 ft of vertical. The mountain biking the town is known for is mostly in the Questa Ranger District of the Carson National Forest around it rather than a built, lift-served park on the ski hill - the resort publishes no bike trail list or summer bike ticket.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No published lift-served bike operation.</b> The forest trails are pedal-access.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer and autumn at altitude.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Taos</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr><tr><td>Santa Fe</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.redriverskiarea.com/">Red River Ski and Summer Area</a> and <a href="https://redriver.org/things-to-do/bike/">Red River town - biking</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
