  <Placemark>
    <name>Bikepark Kouty (Jeseniky, Czech Republic) [400 CZK]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Kouty nad Desnou 608 m - valley station of the Medvedi hora chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Four marked runs off the biggest lift-served vertical in the Jeseniky, a 500 m drop down a long wooded slope, so these are sustained descents rather than short laps. Uhlirska is the blue one and the longest at 7 km, an easy flow trail the operator calls a relaxed route for anybody. Hrebenovka (orange, 4.5 km) is the 4X and freeride line, jumps and berms, for riders who already know what they are doing. Stara Medvedice (red, 4 km) is natural ground with roots and technical sections. Koutikuv sen (black, 3 km) is the extreme one and hosts rounds of the Czech DH Cup.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A six-seat chairlift - the operator claims the fastest in the country - from Lisci potok at about 600 m to Medvedi hora at 1100 m. Around 400 CZK for a day; tickets from the kiosks on Koutecky square, where Helia Sport also rents Kona hardtails and full-suspension bikes.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly May to mid-October.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-16:30<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Sumperk</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Olomouc</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h20</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://kouty.cz/bike-park/">Bike Park Kouty</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
