  <Placemark>
    <name>PKL Bike Park Mosorny Gron (Zawoja, Poland) [69 PLN]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Zawoja 715 m - valley station of the Mosorny Gron chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Three downhill trails straight off the chairlift, and close to 20 km of riding once you add the neighbouring Babia Gora Trails. Rydzowy is the green - hardened, evenly graded, no difficult obstacles. Sokolica is the blue, also hardened but wanting basic bike-handling. Wilcza Lapa is the red, and it is natural ground: no surfacing, real terrain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A chairlift to the summit. One PKL bike pass covers four resorts - Mosorny Gron, Gora Zar, Palenica and Butorowy Wierch - and includes third-party and accident insurance for riding the trails. From September to the end of the season a day pass drops to 69 PLN online or at the ticket office. Ten-ride cards are also sold.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly May to the end of October.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Bielsko-Biala</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Krakow</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.pkl.pl/mosorny-gron/trasy-rowerowe.html">PKL Mosorny Gron trails</a> and <a href="https://rowery.pkl.pl/">PKL Bike Parks</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
