  <Placemark>
    <name>Zahar Berkut Bike Park (Volosianka, Ukraine) [300 UAH]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Volosianka 671 m - valley station of the Zahar Berkut chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A bike park on the summer side of a Carpathian ski complex at Volosianka, spread over the slopes of Zvorets (1223 m) and Vysokyi Verkh (1224 m). The resort's own description of the summer offer is short - the bike park plus an outdoor pool - so treat the trail count as unconfirmed and expect ski-slope gravity riding rather than a shaped park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Ukraine's longest passenger cable car, a 2800 m two-seat chairlift, plus three drag lifts of 700, 740 and 820 m. The lifts carry bikes in summer. A return sightseeing ticket is around 300 UAH; the lifts run 09:00-17:00.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer, alongside the resort's other warm-season activities.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-17:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Slavske</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Lviv</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://guide.karpaty.ua/uk/places/zachar-berkut">Karpaty guide - Zakhar Berkut</a> and <a href="https://zymaghory.com/tourism/volosyanka/ukr">Zymaghory - Volosianka</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
