  <Placemark>
    <name>Oppdal Bike Park (Trondelag, Norway) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Hovden, Oppdal 589 m - valley station of the Hovden-expressen</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>About 7 marked runs on the Hovden side of the Oppdal ski area, on close to 490 m of lift-served vertical - a genuinely big drop, and one of the longest lift-served descents in Norway outside Hafjell and Trysil. Open fjell terrain above the treeline at the top.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Hovden-expressen chairlift from 589 m to about 1078 m; the Hakerekspressen and Stolen lifts serve the rest of the mountain. Check the operator for the summer bike ticket.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly mid-June to mid-September.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:00<br/><small>Estimated; not yet checked against the operator.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Trondheim</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h45</td></tr><tr><td>Oppdal station</td><td>Train + bus</td><td>~20 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://oppdal.com/">Visit Oppdal</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
