  <Placemark>
    <name>Plattekill Bike Park (Catskills, New York) [35 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Roxbury 701 m - valley station of the Northface double chair</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A long-running Catskills downhill hill with a serious reputation. The directory lists it twice, at 11 and 36 runs, with at least 2 green, 3 blue and 3 black; roughly 310 m of lift-served vertical on steep, raw, rocky New York terrain. Old-school downhill rather than a flow park, and famously cheap for what it is.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Northface double chair from 701 m to about 1013 m, with the Sunshine triple on the other side. Around 35 USD for a day.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly mid-May to mid-October, mostly weekends.<br/>Daily opening hours: 09:00-16:00<br/><small>Estimated; not yet checked against the operator.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Albany</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr><tr><td>New York City</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://plattekill.com/">Plattekill Mountain</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
