  <Placemark>
    <name>Grouse Mountain Bike Park (North Vancouver, BC) [84 CAD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>North Vancouver 301 m - valley station of the Blue Grouse gondola</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The North Shore's only chairlift-accessed bike park, and a new one: seven trails plus a dedicated learning zone, running from green and blue flow lines to advanced and expert terrain. Gravity Logic - the crew behind Whistler Bike Park - built it, and every trail feeds back to the Screaming Eagle chairlift.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Screaming Eagle chairlift. Adult day ticket 84 CAD, or 69 CAD for BC residents; season passes from 499 CAD adult and 299 CAD child.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>June to October.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Vancouver downtown</td><td>Bus + Seabus</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Vancouver downtown</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.grousemountain.com/bike-park">Grouse Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://www.grousemountain.com/bike-park/buy-bike-day-tickets-rentals">Grouse Bike Park day tickets</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
