  <Placemark>
    <name>WinSport Bike Park (Calgary, Alberta) [59 CAD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Canada Olympic Park 1130 m - valley station of the Legacy Express</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Around 31 marked runs with at least 8 green, 16 blue and 5 black - a dense, heavily built park on the 1988 Olympic hill inside Calgary. Only about 110 m of vertical, so it is all lap count, jump lines and progression, with a dirt-jump and skills area alongside.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>The Legacy Express and '88 Express chairs from 1130 m to about 1239 m. Around 59 CAD for a day.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The directory gives a 24 June start; roughly late June to the end of September.<br/>Daily opening hours: 12:00-20:00<br/><small>Season start from the directory listing; hours estimated.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Calgary downtown</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Banff</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.winsport.ca/">WinSport</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
