  <Placemark>
    <name>Taos Bike Park (New Mexico) [25 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Taos Ski Valley 2878 m - valley station of Lift 1</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Downhill flow trails off Lift 4 at Taos Ski Valley, graded for every level, at an altitude that will remind you where you are. Behind The Bavarian there is a free skills park, built as a low-pressure place to work on fundamentals before committing to the mountain.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Lift 4. Bike-park lift tickets are 25 USD a day, or 15 USD for Millennium and Full Pass holders - cheap by American resort standards.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Daily 27 June to 7 September, 10:00-16:30, weather permitting.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:30<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Taos</td><td>Car</td><td>~35 min</td></tr><tr><td>Santa Fe</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.skitaos.com/biking">Taos Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://taosskivalley.com/member/kachina-basin-activities/">Taos Ski Valley summer activities</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
