  <Placemark>
    <name>Snow Summit Bike Park - Big Bear (California) [39-65 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Snow Summit 2131 m - valley station of Chair 1, the bike-park chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Southern California's main lift-served park, at 8200 ft above Big Bear Lake, with nearly ten years of trail building behind it and a clear character: jump lines and airtime rather than raw downhill, which suits riders working on style more than racers. Beginner, intermediate and advanced downhill trails are backed by a Skill Builder Park holding jump, pro and pump lines, and the 10-Ply DH track gives the steeper end something. From the top you also reach a long cross-country network on the same ticket - the Skyline Ridge Trail (2N10) runs across the resort with views to San Gorgonio and the lake, and Pine Knot and Cougar Crest add several more miles of singletrack. Snow Valley across the valley is part of the same pass.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Chairs 1 and 2 haul bikes from the Snow Summit base. Day passes start at 39 USD and run to 65 USD depending on the day and how far ahead they are bought; single rides, sold at the window only, are 23-44 USD for 13 and over and 16-30 USD for ages 5-12, free for under-5s and over-80s. Afternoon tickets run 33-63 USD. Ticketing is shared with Snow Valley under Big Bear Mountain Resort.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The Californian summer season; Snow Summit runs daily, Snow Valley on selected dates only.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Big Bear Lake</td><td>Car</td><td>~5 min</td></tr><tr><td>San Bernardino</td><td>Car</td><td>~1 h 15</td></tr><tr><td>Los Angeles</td><td>Car</td><td>~2 h 30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.bigbearmountainresort.com/mountain-biking">Big Bear Mountain Resort - mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://www.bigbearmountainresort.com/mountain-biking/lift-tickets">Snow Valley + Summit Bike Park - lift tickets</a>. Pin on <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/257997025">OSM way 257997025</a>, the lower end of Chair 1. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
