  <Placemark>
    <name>Mount Baldy (California) [summer lift ticket]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Mount Baldy 1977 m - valley station of chair 1</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Read this one carefully before committing a day to it. Mt Baldy runs its chairlifts through the summer and sells unlimited-ride passes, and riders do use them, but the resort markets the warm season around hiking, the view from Top of the Notch and the lodge rather than around a built bike park - there is no published trail list, grading or bike-park page. Treat it as lift-served mountain terrain rather than a shaped park, and confirm bike carriage before you drive up.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Chairs 1 and 4 run in summer with unlimited rides on a day ticket; the resort also sells a year-round pass covering all four seasons.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer and autumn.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Los Angeles</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr><tr><td>Ontario, CA</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.mtbaldyresort.com/tickets">The Lifts at Mt Baldy - tickets</a> and <a href="https://www.mtbaldyresort.com/season-passes">Mt Baldy season passes</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
