  <Placemark>
    <name>West Mountain Bike Park (New York) [30 USD, suspended for 2026]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Queensbury 131 m - valley station of the West Express</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Over twenty cross-country and downhill trails on the hill above Queensbury - around five miles of trail and a lot of repeat descending for the vertical. <b>Check before travelling: West Mountain decided not to run mountain biking for the summer of 2026.</b> The trails and the chairlift are still there, and the resort has run the park in past summers, so this may be a pause rather than an ending - but do not assume it is open.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A chairlift, when the bike park runs. The day ticket was 30 USD.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Historically from 1 July; suspended for summer 2026.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Glens Falls</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Albany</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://westmountain.com/mountain-biking/">West Mountain mountain biking</a> and <a href="https://westmountain.com/lift-tickets/">West Mountain lift tickets</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
