  <Placemark>
    <name>Mont du Lac Resort (Superior, Wisconsin) [free trails]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Superior 196 m - valley station of the chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Five miles and more of singletrack loops above the St Louis river, intermediate to advanced, with steep climbs and fast descents and views over Jay Cooke State Park. The resort packages it with a waterpark, disc golf and an archery range.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift.</b> The trails are free to ride, and a shuttle runs every Tuesday and Sunday, weather permitting. Summer day passes and season passes cover the resort's other activities; guest services on +1 218 626 3797 has the rates.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>The summer season.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Duluth</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Minneapolis</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.mdlresort.com/tickets-passes">Mont du Lac Resort - tickets and passes</a> and <a href="https://gottabesuperior.com/what-to-do/trails/">Superior, WI - trails</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
