  <Placemark>
    <name>Parc du Mont St-Mathieu (Quebec) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Saint-Mathieu-de-Rioux 124 m - valley station of the chairlift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Six descent trails and an enduro line, more than 13 km in all, on a hill between Rimouski and Riviere-du-Loup. The progression is deliberate - green trails that genuinely work for beginners at one end, intense double blacks at the other - and the harder ground has steep switchbacks, technical sections, jumps and rock.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A chairlift. Day tickets and season passes by age band, including student, adult and senior rates; buying online saves about five percent. Shop, workshop, rental and food on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer and autumn.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Rimouski</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Quebec City</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h45</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://montstmathieu.com/velo_de_montagne/">Parc du Mont St-Mathieu - velo de montagne</a> and <a href="https://montstmathieu.com/velo_de_montagne/acces-tarification/">Mont St-Mathieu access and pricing</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
