  <Placemark>
    <name>Sunlight Mountain (Colorado) [check operator]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sunlight 2483 m - valley station of the Segundo chair</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A small, cheap, unpretentious hill above Glenwood Springs - 75 runs over 680 acres in winter and no lift queues - that keeps a mountain and road biking page for the warm season. The resort does not publish a graded bike-park trail list, so treat this as summer riding on ski-area terrain and the Glenwood trails around it rather than a built gravity park, and check what is actually turning before you go.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Summer lift operations are not published as a bike-park product; ask the resort.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Summer, subject to what the resort chooses to run.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Glenwood Springs</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Denver</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://sunlightmtn.com/">Sunlight Mountain Resort</a> and <a href="https://sunlightmtn.com/plan-your-trip/buy-lift-ticket">Sunlight Mountain tickets</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
