  <Placemark>
    <name>Hammarbybacken Bike Park (Stockholm, Sweden) [150 SEK]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Stockholm 14 m - valley station of the Globen drag lift</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Eight downhill runs from green to black on the artificial hill in southern Stockholm, with the green machine-built and wide enough that a beginner and a fast rider can share it. Downhill has been ridden here since 2003, and the trails and the anchor lift have been kept going by the club Sthlms Friakare rather than by the resort - worth knowing, because SkiStar's shift towards other summer attractions has put the downhill operation in doubt more than once. Confirm the lift is turning before you make the trip.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>An anchor lift. Day pass around 150 SEK, evening pass 120 SEK.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>1 May to 31 October, normally afternoons into the evening.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Stockholm centre</td><td>Metro + walk</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Stockholm centre</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.skistar.com/sv/hammarbybacken/sommar-i-hammarbybacken/">SkiStar Hammarbybacken summer</a> and <a href="https://www.skistar.com/sv/hammarbybacken/planera/biljetter-och-priser/">SkiStar Hammarbybacken tickets</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
