  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Molini di Triora Freeride (Liguria) [commercial shuttle]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Molini di Triora 444 m - bottom of the Molini Freeriders descents</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>An enduro area rather than a park: dense singletrack, built and natural, through pine woods in the Valle Argentina at the foot of the Maritime Alps, with flow lines among the technical ground. It is one of the established Ligurian winter-riding destinations, which is why so many operators run here.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift - shuttles.</b> Several outfits serve the valley, among them Freeride Spirit, Omnia Freeride, Molini MTB and aTIPICO, most offering guided days and multi-day packages as well as plain uplift. Book ahead.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year round - the Ligurian coast is a winter destination as much as a summer one.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Sanremo</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr><tr><td>Imperia</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.molinimtb.com/">Molini MTB</a>, <a href="https://omniafreeride.com/en/trails">Omnia Freeride</a> and <a href="https://www.atipicooutdoorescape.com/">aTIPICO Outdoor Escape</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
