  <Placemark>
    <name>Bikepark Tres Cantos (Madrid, Spain) [5 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Tres Cantos 699 m - the municipal bike park north of Madrid</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Around 11 marked runs, at least 1 green and 3 blue. This is a built municipal park on flat ground rather than a hillside - jump lines, berms, pump and dirt-jump areas, with the shaping providing the gradient. OpenStreetMap tags the site itself Bike Park.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and effectively no hill: you push or pedal back up. Around 5 EUR entry.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open year-round; the limiting factor is the Madrid summer heat rather than snow.<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Estimated; not yet checked against the operator.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Madrid centre</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Tres Cantos station</td><td>Cercanias + bike</td><td>~15 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://web.trescantos.es/">Ayuntamiento de Tres Cantos</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
