  <Placemark>
    <name>Racepark Schulenberg (Harz, Germany) [25 EUR]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Schulenberg 432 m - bottom of the race tracks in the Oberharz</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>About 8 marked runs above the Okertalsperre reservoir, at least 2 blue. This is a long-standing German downhill racing venue rather than a flow park. OpenStreetMap carries a very dense graded network across the surrounding Harz forest, from roughly 430 m to 590 m.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Uplift is by shuttle, around 25 EUR for a day.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly April to the end of October.<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Estimated; not yet checked against the operator. Race and shuttle days are usually scheduled rather than daily.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Goslar</td><td>Car</td><td>~25 min</td></tr><tr><td>Hannover</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.outdoorwerkstatt.eu/">Racepark Schulenberg</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
