  <Placemark>
    <name>Bikepark Attendorn (Sauerland, Germany) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Attendorn 361 m - the bike park above the Biggesee</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>One marked blue run, with a singletrail alongside it in OpenStreetMap and a graded network reaching about 460 m on the surrounding Sauerland ridges. A small local spot rather than a destination.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift; pedal or shuttle. The directory lists no price.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Roughly mid-March to mid-November.<br/>Daily opening hours: daylight hours<br/><small>Estimated; not yet checked against the operator.</small><br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Attendorn</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Cologne</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h15</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Source: <a href="https://www.attendorn.de/">Hansestadt Attendorn</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
