  <Placemark>
    <name>Heidenloch Bikepark (Braunlingen, Black Forest) [no lift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Braunlingen 852 m - the Heidenloch bike park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A small park that gets more out of its ground than the size suggests - the Baden cycling association rates it highly for variety in a confined space and recommends it for families, beginners and mixed-ability groups. The trails are natural and threaded between rock and rooted forest floor, with drops, rock sections, steep banked corners, tight turns and bridges. By the barbecue hut there is a pump track, the Kohlemeiler ramp, the Brandbach wave and a small skills station.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift.</b> Pedal up; the descents are short enough that laps are the point.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Open outside the winter rest, which runs 1 November to 31 March.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Donaueschingen</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Freiburg</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://heidenloch-bikepark.de/">Heidenloch-Bikepark</a> and <a href="https://www.schwarzwald-tourismus.info/attraktionen/heidenloch-bikepark-6985b849d4">Schwarzwald Tourismus</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
