  <Placemark>
    <name>Kelly Canyon Bike Park (Idaho) [30 USD]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Kelly Canyon 1771 m - valley station of the Gold Rush chair</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Nineteen miles of trail sorted into three honest categories: Road, the fire roads crossing the national forest; Mowed, trails literally mown into existence; and Code, the built lines with banked turns and rollers. It is a small resort being upfront about what it has, which is refreshing.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>Lift-served Thursday to Sunday, 10 to 30 USD depending on age and half or full day. Sunday to Wednesday you can still ride the trails without the lift by paying at the self-serve box on site. Hardtail rental 20-35 USD, helmets 11 USD, available Thursday to Saturday.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>From 30 June through the summer.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Idaho Falls</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr><tr><td>Jackson, WY</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.kellycanyonresort.com/bike-park/">Kelly Canyon Resort bike park</a> and <a href="https://visitidaho.org/travel-tips/a-beginners-guide-to-mountain-biking-at-kelly-canyon/">Visit Idaho beginner guide</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
