  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Kjerringasen Bikepark (Sarpsborg, Norway) [280 NOK]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Kjerringasen 182 m - the alpine centre above Sarpsborg</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A small park in the middle of Ostfold built for riders who like speed, with Gubben - 1200 m - as the signature run and UK-style grading across the rest. It is volunteer-run, and the volunteers walk the trails every spring clearing deadfall, filling holes and repairing winter damage. Norgescup downhill rounds have been decided here.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A lift, which has had its share of unscheduled failures - the club has had to delay season openings because of it, so check before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>From May. Lift Saturdays and Sundays 11:00-17:00.<br/>Daily opening hours: 11:00-17:00<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Sarpsborg</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Oslo</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.terrengsykkel.no/utfor/kjerringaasen">Terrengsykkel on Kjerringasen</a> and <a href="https://www.facebook.com/kjerringaasendownhill/">Kjerringasen Sykkelpark</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
