  <Placemark>
    <name>Okeford Hill Bike Park (Dorset, England) [25 GBP uplift]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Okeford Hill 223 m - the bike park on the Dorset chalk ridge</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Seven or eight downhill trails over 22 hectares of the Dorset chalk ridge, with about 125 m of drop - the park calls it alpine-style, and over 400 feet of continuous descent in southern England is worth the claim. The ground is earth, chalk and flint, built up with rock gardens, berms, tabletops and drops, and steep rooty technical sections where the hill allows.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A Land Rover and bike trailer, with bikes strapped on and checked by the driver before each run - efficient enough for about twenty runs in a day. Around 15 GBP for a half day and 25 GBP for a full day.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Wednesday to Sunday.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Blandford Forum</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Bournemouth</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.okefordhillbikepark.com/">Okeford Hill Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://www.okefordhillbikepark.com/uplift">Okeford Hill uplift</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
