  <Placemark>
    <name>Isle of Wight Mountain Bike Centre (England) [day permit]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Shorwell 75 m - the Isle of Wight Mountain Bike Centre</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The only trail centre on the island, on Cheverton Farm near Shorwell and running since 2011. Eight trails covering blue, red and black, laid out so you can build your own loop: the 3.5 km Green Loop is family ground with an all-weather surface, and the 9 km Blue Loop finishes down the Twisted Wizard descent. Technical sections, jumps and flow depending on which way you link them.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift</b> - pedal-up loops. A day or season permit is required and the money goes to trail maintenance and public liability cover. This is private farmland, so you must pay and accept the terms before riding.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year round.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Newport, IoW</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Southampton</td><td>Ferry + car</td><td>~1h30</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.isleofwightmountainbikecentre.com/">Isle of Wight Mountain Bike Centre</a> and <a href="http://www.cyclewight.org.uk/iw-mtb-centre.html">CycleWight</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
