  <Placemark>
    <name>Nant Gwrtheyrn (Llithfaen, Wales) [26 GBP]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Nant Gwrtheyrn 76 m - the valley below Llithfaen, on the Llyn peninsula</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Two black-graded downhill tracks dropping into a former quarry village on the Llyn peninsula, with the sea below you the whole way. The original track hosted a round of the British Downhill Series in 2011 and is steep and technical; a second, easier line has since been added. This is a hill for experienced riders on capable bikes with proper protection.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>Uplift days only</b> - the tracks are not open to ride outside them. Simply Downhill run a minibus and purpose-built bike trailer, 10:00 to 16:30, and sixteen to eighteen runs in a day is normal. Booking is through the British Cycling website, online payment only. Riders must be 12 or over, and under-18s need an adult with them. Cafe on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Scheduled uplift days through the year.<br/>Daily opening hours: 10:00-16:30<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Caernarfon</td><td>Car</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Bangor</td><td>Car</td><td>~50 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://nantgwrtheyrn.org/">Nant Gwrtheyrn</a> and <a href="https://www.trailguru.co.uk/mountain-biking-nant-gwrtheyrn/">TrailGuru on Nant Gwrtheyrn</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
