  <Placemark>
    <name>Zilina Oko Trails (Slovakia) [free]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Zilina 648 m - the Oko trail network above the city</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Ten trails through forest on the hillside overlooking Zilina, and the first legal trail park in the district - built by Michal Kolar, Martin Knapec and Simon Rus with the OKO Everywhere group, and funded by the riding community rather than an operator. Grades run from recreational to serious enough that the Slovak enduro championships have been raced here. Coaching runs regularly from April to September.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift.</b> Free to ride, community-funded - which means the trails exist because riders maintain them.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Spring to autumn.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Zilina centre</td><td>Bike</td><td>~30 min</td></tr><tr><td>Bratislava</td><td>Car</td><td>~2h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://okoeverywhere.com/oko-trails/">Zilina OKO Trails</a> and <a href="https://www.regionmalafatra.sk/en/bike-parks-and-sports-zones/zilina-oko-trails-2/">Region Mala Fatra</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
