  <Placemark>
    <name>Bike Park des Lacs de l'Eau d'Heure (Belgium) [day access]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Lacs de l'Eau d'Heure 235 m - the bike park by the reservoirs</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The most complete gravity site in Wallonia, in the middle of the Eau d'Heure lakes: eleven multi-discipline trails at every grade and more than 30 km of riding, plus trial zones, freeride and dirt areas served by a mechanical tow, a dual slalom, a big air bag and a pump track. A bike wash on site.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>A mechanical lift serves the descents, with a separate tow for the dirt and freeride area. There is one ticket and one price - a day pass, booked online - and it is yours whether you stay two hours or all day.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Through the riding season; book before travelling.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Charleroi</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Brussels</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h20</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://naturaparc.be/fr/bike-park-lacs-eau-d-heure">Natura Parc - Bike Park des Lacs</a> and <a href="https://www.lacsdeleaudheure.be/en/activities/bike-park">Domaine des Lacs de l'Eau d'Heure</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
