  <Placemark>
    <name>Lincoln Bike Park (California, United States) [free]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>California 43 m - Lincoln Bike Park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>A community park in Foskett Park north of Sacramento, run by a non-profit and still being built out. Three features are open: a dirt pump track, a progressive flow line and a skinny-and-technical section, with a skills course and further pump tracks planned. Flat valley ground, so everything here is shaped.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift and no hill - you pedal round.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year-round, sunrise to sunset. Free to the public except when leagues, events or training sessions are running.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Sacramento</td><td>Car</td><td>~40 min</td></tr><tr><td>Roseville</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://lincolnbikepark.com/">Lincoln Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/1539333644">OSM way 1539333644</a> (ODbL). Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
