  <Placemark>
    <name>Hinton Bike Park (Alberta, Canada) [free]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Alberta 1083 m - Hinton Bike Park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>The park sits at over 1000 m on the eastern approach to Jasper, and is one piece of a much larger picture: the Hinton Mountain Bike Association maintains roughly 90 km of trail across the Bighorn Ridge, Happy Creek, Jack's and Nordic Centre networks. The association does not publish a per-trail difficulty breakdown, so the gravity content here is not yet quantified.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/>No lift. Pedal or shuttle the forest roads.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Estimated from latitude and altitude - roughly mid-May to mid-October.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Hinton</td><td>Car</td><td>~10 min</td></tr><tr><td>Jasper</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr><tr><td>Edmonton</td><td>Car</td><td>~3h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.bikehinton.com/">Hinton Mountain Bike Association</a> and <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/424436586">OSM way 424436586</a> (ODbL). Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
