  <Placemark>
    <name>Mont Poupet Bike Park (Jura, France) [free]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Jura 842 m - Mount Poupet Bike Park</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Seven enduro trails around Mont Poupet above Salins-les-Bains, from 2.5 to 4 km with about 350 m of descent, and the building philosophy is restraint: the lines are natural, worked only where they have to be, so the speed comes from the shape of the ground rather than from shaping. The FFCT base circuits run past the Saint-Andre and Belin forts above the town.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No lift, and the trails are free all year.</b> The climb is a 5 km paved road, which makes pedalling up simple if slow - about 45 minutes. The Mont Poupet BikePark association organises shuttles and sells memberships if you would rather not.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year round, free access.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Salins-les-Bains</td><td>Car</td><td>~15 min</td></tr><tr><td>Besancon</td><td>Car</td><td>~45 min</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.montpoupetbikepark.fr/">Mont Poupet Bike Park</a> and <a href="https://www.jura-tourism.com/activite/mont-poupet-bike-park/">Jura Tourisme</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
