  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Wharncouver (Sheffield, England) [free]</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Sheffield 194 m - Wharncouver</b><br/><br/>
    <b>Trails</b><br/>Wharncliffe Woods is a steep, rocky wood on the northern edge of Sheffield with a downhill scene going back decades - it is where Steve Peat learned to ride, and it is known for technical rock drops. Wharncouver, the red-graded centrepiece sometimes called Mini-Whistler, is the volunteer-built progression line with berms, big features and hip jumps; the wider network runs to dozens of trails, among them Vajazzle, Fergs Varsity, Diamond Back, Rake and Bake and Truffle Shuffle. <b>Unofficial:</b> these are rider-built trails on Forestry England land and have been bulldozed before, so what is there changes.<br/><br/>
    <b>Getting up / price</b><br/><b>No uplift.</b> Pedal up, free to ride.<br/><br/>
    <b>Open season</b><br/>Year round; the woods drain reasonably but the rock is slick in the wet.<br/><br/>
    <b>Access</b><table class="access"><tr><th>From</th><th>Transport</th><th>Duration</th></tr><tr><td>Sheffield</td><td>Car</td><td>~20 min</td></tr><tr><td>Manchester</td><td>Car</td><td>~1h00</td></tr></table><br/>
    <i>Sources: <a href="https://www.singletraction.co.uk/wp/?page_id=374">SingletrAction, the local trail association</a>, <a href="https://enduro-mtb.com/en/scene-visit-wharncliffe-woods-sheffield-uk/">Enduro Mountainbike Magazine scene visit</a> and <a href="https://off.road.cc/content/news/wharncliffe-woods-trails-flattened-by-forestry-commission-3022">off.road.cc on the Forestry Commission clearance</a>. Prices, schedules, trail status and access can change; verify before travel.</i>]]></description>
    <styleUrl>#placemark-brown</styleUrl>
